      "title": "Computer Technician",
      "description": "Computer Technician - Sandwich Placement | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Computer Technician - Sandwich Placement Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Computer Technician - Sandwich Placement Fixed-term: 1 year. There are three positions available from August/September. They are at the Departments of Chemistry and Earth Sciences and the Faculty of Mathematics. The exact start dates will be by negotiation. The Department of Earth Sciences is the top Earth Science department in the 2016 Complete University Guide for the UK, in international league tables we are consistently listed in the top five. The role of IT is central to much of the research carried out in the department, this includes developing sophisticated computer models of how the Earth works and interrogating large datasets produced from instrumentation in our labs. The Faculty of Mathematics is one of the world's leading centres for teaching and research in mathematics. Our researchers work across pure and applied mathematics, statistics and theoretical physics. Their work ranges from exploring number theory and the origins of the universe to improving healthcare and understanding climate change. Computers and IT are essential to much of this research. They allow researchers to create mathematical models and simulations, develop specialist software, use machine learning and analyse large amounts of data. The Yusuf Hamied Department of Chemistry enjoys a world class reputation as a centre of excellence for Chemical Research and Teaching. This is underpinned by the application of wide range of IT technologies and solutions to meet the aims of the Department. We wish to appoint three trainee students, one each in the Departments of Chemistry and Earth Sciences and one in the Faculty of Mathematics, to provide IT support to the community of researchers, students and support staff.\nThe key responsibilities of the roles include: Share in staffing the Help Desk with other members of the team: triaging the problems as they come in and assigning them to the appropriate support queue or person. Perform first line support duties chiefly but not exclusively on Linux, Windows and Mac platforms. Perform a share of the procurement, installation, configuration, decommissioning and disposal of desktop hardware. Manage user access to data and resources using the standard tools of the Departments. Develop scripts and code under the guidance of senior technical members of the team to improve delivery of IT services. Assist with the installation, configuration, and disposal of server hardware. These \"Sandwich Student\" roles will provide a great opportunity for a self-starting student to gain valuable work experience in a team supporting a complex environment with real users. The major element of the role will be providing front line support. Training and support will be provided for learning technologies such as Python where appropriate. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For informal queries please contact Emma Graham ( ejg49@cam.ac.uk ). Please quote reference MA51115 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The Yusuf Hamied Department of Chemistry holds an Athena SWAN silver award for women in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics, and Medicine. The Department of Earth Sciences holds an Athena SWAN bronze award for women in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics, and Medicine. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Key information Department/location Yusuf Hamied Department of Chemistry Salary £23,350 Reference MA51115 Category Assistant staff Date published 2 October 2026 Closing date 12 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/data-lifecycle-project-manager-fixed-term-ra51371": {
      "title": "Data Lifecycle Project Manager (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Data Lifecycle Project Manager (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Data Lifecycle Project Manager (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Data Lifecycle Project Manager (Fixed Term) The School of Clinical Medicine wishes to appoint a Data Lifecycle Project Manager to join their Research Governance team. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced and motivated individual to take a lead role in establishing routes for turning highly valuable research data assets into sustainable data products that could be better utilised both internally and by external researchers. Clinical School researchers collect and generate an enormous amount of research data which is stored across various University IT platforms and cloud systems.  On completion of a specific research project there are few resources to maintain and access these data assets further for the benefit of other researchers both within and external to the University.  In essence few of these research datasets are FAIR (Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, Reusable). This fixed term full-time role will actively look at data sets held across the Clinical School, liaise with Cambridge University Hospitals (CUH) Research & Development team, the Clinical School Research Governance team and the Research Office to put together a policy and manual for researchers to enable these collated data sets to be sustainably managed throughout the data lifecycle and FAIR. The role sits within the University Clinical Governance team but will require close liaison with the University Research Operations Office, the School of Clinical Medicine Computing Service (CSCS) and the University Information Services (UIS) within the University. The role holder will also need to liaise with other institutions on the Biomedical Campus including CUH R&D, Cambridge and Peterborough Foundation Trust R&D office and Cambridge University Health Partners. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 12 months in the first instance. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter and CV in the Upload section of the online application. The covering letter should outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference RA51371 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars (RA51371) Key information Department/location Office of the School of Clinical Medicine Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference RA51371 Category Academic-related Date published 12 October 2026 Closing date 4 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/deputy-biofacility-managernacwo-aq51227": {
      "title": "Deputy Biofacility Manager/NACWO",
      "description": "Deputy Biofacility Manager/NACWO | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Deputy Biofacility Manager/NACWO Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Deputy Biofacility Manager/NACWO We are currently looking for a Deputy Bio facility Manager within UBS. Applications are invited for a motivated and experienced Chief Animal Technician/Deputy Manager to be part of a hard working team in a busy biomedical services facility situated in South Cambridge. The successful candidate will assist the Biofacility Manager with the day to day management of the facility and deputise in their absence.  As Deputy Manager, the successful candidate will co-ordinate the animal husbandry work of the facility. You will assist the Biofacility Manager with the recruitment, training and assessment of new staff with in-house policies and procedures as well as working to Home Office regulations and performance management. You will manage both licenced and unlicensed scientific procedures along with daily husbandry and maintenance to assist the technicians as required. You are responsible for the maintenance of all necessary records, referring any issues and concerns to the Biofacility Manager as necessary. This will include the use of IVC technology, supervision of day to day husbandry, breeding, maintenance and genotyping of genetically modified animals. Checking and recording environmental parameters and general condition of animals will be required on a daily basis. The role holder will act as Named Animal Care and Welfare Officer (NACWO) for an area of the facility, and shall be the primary point of contact for the Project and Personal Licence holders, providing advice and guidance regarding Home Office regulations, reviewing study plans to ensure appropriate allocation of resources and compliance. You will be able to work both independently and as part of a team, with experience supervising or managing staff. You will have IAT Level 3 or equivalent, Home Office Licence modules A-C and will be a Personal Licence holder. In depth experience of working within a biofacility is essential, as are excellent communication skills. You must be able to use a computerised data management system and have previous experience working in a supervisory / team leader role. Knowledge of relevant Home Office, and Health and Safety legislation is important, as is knowledge and experience in the principals of aseptic surgery and specialised breeding techniques. The facility operates a rota system to provide animal care and essential husbandry at weekends and over Bank Holidays. The role holder will be required to be on an out of hours call out list. In addition to the base salary stated above, the successful candidate for this post will receive an additional 2.5% supplement to their pay. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment and a security check. Please quote reference AQ51227 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location University Biomedical Services Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference AQ51227 Category Assistant staff Date published 29 September 2026 Closing date 20 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/deputy-head-of-counselling-and-wellbeing-aw50999": {
      "title": "Deputy Head of Counselling and Wellbeing",
      "description": "Deputy Head of Counselling and Wellbeing | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Deputy Head of Counselling and Wellbeing Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Deputy Head of Counselling and Wellbeing The University Counselling and Wellbeing Service (Student Support) is a dynamic, high-demand service driven by our mission to support and empower students in fulfilling their academic and personal potential. We are at an exciting stage of the service's development. Following a transformative Student Mental Health and Wellbeing Plan (2022-2025) at the Collegiate University, we are recruiting to a number of roles to support our service's work and objectives under a new Student Support strategic plan (2026-2029). As part of an integrated Student Support Department, we work in partnership with the Mental Health Advice Service, the Harassment and Violence Support Service, and the Accessibility and Disability Resource to offer students joined-up support. These services contribute to a wider stepped care approach at Collegiate Cambridge, working in partnership with College Health and Wellbeing teams who support students in their College community. We are seeking to appoint two highly-motivated, experienced professionals in the field of counselling and psychotherapy to the new role of Deputy Head of Counselling and Wellbeing (Student Support). The Deputy Head of Counselling and Wellbeing is a senior, dynamic leadership role. The successful candidate will work in close partnership with the Head of Counselling and Wellbeing and a second Deputy Head of Counselling and Wellbeing, who alongside the Senior Counsellor (Access and Wellbeing) form the management team of the University Counselling and Wellbeing Service. This varied role combines leadership oversight of service operations in line with high professional and ethical standards, leading strategic programmes and service developments, compassionate and effective leadership for staff, and strategic contribution to a service committed to delivering the highest standards of best practice in counselling and psychological therapies. Please note that this post requires accreditation (or registration, where this confers an accreditation-level standard) with your appropriate professional regulatory body in the UK, such as BACP, UKCP, BABCP or HCPC. We particularly encourage candidates from a Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic background to apply for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level within our University. Benefits of working at the University of Cambridge include: Competitive rates of pay with automatic service-related pay progression and annual cost of living increases; Generous annual leave allowance; Flexible and hybrid working opportunities; Generous maternity, adoption and shared parental leave entitlement and other family friendly schemes (e.g. workplace nurseries); An auto-enrolment pension scheme, with a generous employer contribution; Travel benefits and retail discounts at over 2,000 local and national stores; Schemes to support with relocation / the provision of accommodation The interview date for the post is Friday 6th November 2026 When applying, please upload your CV and cover letter outlining how you meet the criteria set out in the person specification in the Further Particulars. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact SSCjobs@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference AW50999 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Deputy Head of Counselling and Wellbeing Key information Department/location Student Support Salary £47,389-£59,966 Reference AW50999 Category Academic-related Date published 1 October 2026 Closing date 22 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/deputy-secretary-school-of-the-physical-sciences-temporary-cover-internal-applicants-only-ak50863": {
      "title": "Deputy Secretary, School of the Physical Sciences [Temporary Cover] (Internal Applicants Only)",
      "description": "Deputy Secretary, School of the Physical Sciences [Temporary Cover] (Internal Applicants Only) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Deputy Secretary, School of the Physical Sciences [Temporary Cover] (Internal Applicants Only) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Deputy Secretary, School of the Physical Sciences [Temporary Cover] (Internal Applicants Only) We are looking for a skilled administrator and manager to join our small and friendly team. You will be an integral member of the team, and of the leadership of the School, supporting the School Secretary across the range of strategic issues the School faces. You will also work closely with the Deputy Head of School for Education on the broad Education portfolio, as well as leading the operational side of the School Office team. There is also the opportunity to take forward specific projects which can be shaped by the interests of the role holder, but might include working with particular Departments, specific policy issues, support for the postgraduate widening participation agenda, or contributing to the development of the new Rokos School of Government. This is an excellent chance for a talented individual to advance their career. The School Office provides a unique perspective on the operation of the University, sitting at an interesting interface between the academic Departments of the School, who are at the forefront of delivering exceptionally high-quality teaching and ground-breaking research, and the University's central administration. We also collaborate directly with external bodies such as funders, especially the Engineering and Physical Sciences Research Council. The role requires experience of staff management and managing change, but most of all the ability to pick-up new issues, in policy or operations, and take them forward to the benefit of the School and its Departments. Candidates should be qualified to at least first degree level or have equivalent professional experience. A qualification in a Physical Science subject is emphatically not a requirement for the post. This opportunity is open to current University of Cambridge employees only. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. Temporary cover: This post is fixed-term until 30 September 2027 or the return of the post holder, whichever is the earlier. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check. Why Join Us? In joining the School of the Physical Sciences, you will not only be part of collaborative and forward-thinking teams that support world-class research, but you will also be part of a welcoming and inclusive workplace with excellent opportunities for professional development. The School offers flexible and hybrid working opportunities. The University of Cambridge is committed to supporting staff to thrive professionally and personally and offers a wide range of benefits https://www.hr.admin.cam.ac.uk/pay-benefits/cambens-employee-benefits Additional information regarding the role may be found within the Further Particulars via the link below. Your CV, along with a covering letter, should clearly set out how you meet the criteria listed in the person specification (the skills and experience required for the role) including relevant examples. Candidates will be shortlisted based upon these criteria. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries about the role should be directed to: Dr Jim Bellingham, School Secretary, Email: SecSPS@admin.cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process, please contact PhysicalSciences@admin.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference AK50863 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information AK50863 - Further Information Key information Department/location Academic Division Salary £47,389-£59,966 Reference AK50863 Category Academic-related Date published 28 August 2026 Closing date 18 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/desktop-service-analyst-fixed-term-vc51279": {
      "title": "Desktop Service Analyst (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Desktop Service Analyst (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Desktop Service Analyst (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Desktop Service Analyst (Fixed Term) University Information Services (UIS), University of Cambridge\nThe University Information Services (UIS) provides the University of Cambridge, its colleges, and associated institutions with a wide and constantly evolving range of IT services supporting administration, research, and teaching. The Infrastructure Division of UIS comprises approximately 100 staff and is responsible for delivering and supporting production services across the collegiate University. Join us on our journey within UIS. About the role We are seeking a Desktop Service Analyst to join our Desktop and Systems Support team. The role will be predominantly based at the Department of Veterinary Medicine, which includes the Queen's Veterinary School Hospital, providing dedicated, high-quality IT support in a diverse and dynamic environment. This is a full-time, primarily on-site role, with the option to work from home one day per week. You will act as a key point of contact for technical queries, delivering both 1st and 2nd line support across a range of IT systems and services. The role offers exposure to a broad variety of environments such as administration, research and clinical, requiring strong problem-solving skills and technical versatility. This post is fixed-term for 2-years in the first instance. Key responsibilities Deliver first, second and, at times, third-line support both on-site and remotely Diagnose, prioritise, and resolve incidents and service requests in line with agreed procedures Act as a primary contact for users via multiple support channels (in person, ITSM tickets, phone, Teams, etc.) Escalate unresolved issues and support service recovery Investigate root causes of incidents and contribute to service improvement Support a wide range of UIS services in a complex, varied IT environment Skills, qualifications and experience Good education to HND or degree level in a relevant subject, or equivalent experience Demonstrable experience in at least two of the following: Microsoft Windows operating systems and applications Apple macOS / iOS Microsoft Intune Microsoft Entra / Azure Microsoft 365 Networking fundamentals Strong troubleshooting skills, particularly in client-server environments Excellent communication and customer service skills Experience of working on and running IT projects up to £10k Self-motivated, adaptable, and able to work both independently and as part of a team Working arrangements Full-time position Based primarily on-site at the Department of Veterinary Medicine Hybrid working available (up to one day per week from home) Interviews are likely to take place week beginning 16 November 2026. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. We particularly welcome applications from women and /or candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our department. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Whilst we may use AI tools as part of our job roles, we want to hear from you in your application.  We strongly discourage the use of artificial intelligence, automated tools, or other third-party assistance to generate, draft, or significantly modify your application. Your CV, along with a covering letter, should clearly set out how you meet the criteria listed in the person specification (the skills and experience required for the role) including relevant examples. Candidates will be shortlisted based upon these criteria. If you would like more information about this role, informal enquiries can be directed by email to recruitment@uis.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference VC51279 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Desktop Service Analyst Further Information Key information Department/location University Information Services Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference VC51279 Category Assistant staff Date published 5 October 2026 Closing date 8 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
