    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-nurse-fixed-term-ps51189": {
      "title": "Research Nurse (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Nurse (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Nurse (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Nurse (Fixed Term) The UK Hub for Predictive and AI-Enabled Human Disease Models is a UK national research initiative funded by the MRC, which will translate academic New Approach Methodologies (NAMs) into validated, industry-ready systems. The Hub brings together leading scientists, clinicians and commercial organisations to drive advances for national benefit. The Hub is based in the Cambridge Stem Cell Institute (CSCI).\nThe role of Research Nurse will be integral to a Hub team established to accelerate the development, validation and adoption of predictive human disease models for biomedical research, drug discovery and experimental medicine. We are looking for an enthusiastic individual with the drive and initiative to work across the diverse responsibilities of the role, that will include supporting clinic patients, recruiting research participants, working closely with nursing/medical/surgical and research teams and interacting with Hub teams from around the UK. The role will also be involved in Patient & Public Involvement & Engagement (PPIE) activities. The role holder will work between the University and Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust and hold an Honorary Contract with the NHS Trust.\nThe successful candidate will hold a first degree in a relevant discipline, and have a current NMC registration, for nursing or midwifery. They will have experience of Good Clinical Practice (GCP) principles and an understanding and communicating research themes to potential donors. They will be comfortable operating in a fast-paced academic environment and able to engage effectively with a wide range of stakeholders including researchers, patients and families, clinicians, funders, and external partners.\nThis is an opportunity to contribute directly to a programme aiming to transform outcomes for patients. The role offers significant scope to shape how a research centre operates, connects, and grows, both within Cambridge and internationally. Full-time (1.0 FTE; change to part time and flexible working arrangements available); Fixed term until 31 March 2030 (in the first instance) Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to: \nAnthea Stanley [Recruiting Manager]\nEmail: ajs333@cam.ac.uk Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment and an enhanced Disclosure and Barring Service check. This appointment also requires NMC Registration and an Honorary Clinical Contract. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. This is an integrated appointment between the University and Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust (\"NHS Trust\"). You will therefore also be issued with an Honorary Clinical Contract by the NHS Trust. You should be aware that if your contract with the NHS Trust is terminated your employment with the University will be terminated, and vice versa. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter, CV and a completed Additional Information for Clinical Researchers form in the Upload section of the online application. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Closing Date: 20/10/2026 Please quote reference PS51189 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Further Information File Key information Department/location Cambridge Stem Cell Institute (SBS) Salary £37,694-£46,049 Reference PS51189 Category Research Date published 24 September 2026 Closing date 20 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
