    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/senior-investment-analyst-yv51214": {
      "title": "Senior Investment Analyst",
      "description": "Senior Investment Analyst | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Senior Investment Analyst Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Senior Investment Analyst The Role The University of Cambridge is seeking a Senior Investment Analyst to lead its Portfolio Performance (Benefits and Scenarios Modelling) function within the University Change Support Office (UCSO). This is a senior analytical role with responsibility for providing decision-ready quantitative insight into the University's major investments and portfolio of change programmes. UCSO provides expertise in change and communications, benefits realisation, portfolio planning, common standards, strategic reporting and business-case appraisal. It supports the Change and Programme Management Board in directing and overseeing the University's portfolio of major change programmes. The post-holder will own the modelling standards, analytical methods and quality assurance arrangements used to assess benefits, costs, risks, interdependencies and return on investment. They will lead the financial assessment of change programme business cases, deliver complex analytical studies and rapid assessments for senior stakeholders, and strengthen modelling capability through practical guidance and training. The role will also provide analytical support to the Office for Investment Oversight and Appraisal, including the development and appraisal of business cases, work relating to the University's future internal accounting system, and tools to support medium-term financial and strategic planning. The post has reporting responsibilities to the Director of Transformation Programmes and the Director of the Office for Investment Oversight and Appraisal. Key responsibilities - Lead the financial assessment of change programme business cases, including benefits, capital costs, income and expenditure impacts, risks, opportunities, affordability and options appraisal - Develop robust medium- and long-term financial models, using scenario testing and risk analysis to support strategic investment decisions - Establish and maintain consistent modelling standards, datasets, dashboards, performance measures and quality assurance arrangements for portfolio reporting and benefits evaluation - Provide independent insight and constructive challenge to programme, project and investment stakeholders, ensuring that assumptions, evidence, costs, benefits and risks are clearly understood - Prepare authoritative reports, presentations and briefing papers for senior leaders and governance committees and develop practical training and guidance in quantitative appraisal methods About you You will: - Have recent experience of building and using sophisticated long-term financial models for investment analysis, financial projections and scenario testing within a large or complex organisation - Bring substantial experience of investment appraisal, business-case development and the application of specialist quantitative expertise to complex and ambiguous problems - Be able to communicate complex analysis clearly to specialist and non-specialist audiences, influence senior stakeholders and governance groups, and work effectively across multidisciplinary teams - Have advanced Excel modelling capability and experience of reporting and data visualisation tools, together with a postgraduate-level qualification, or equivalent professional expertise, in a quantitative discipline - Be highly numerate, evidence-driven and committed to rigorous governance, value for money and continuous improvement The Benefits In return, you will receive an extensive reward and benefits package including: - 41 days annual leave, including bank holidays - Potential for flexible and hybrid working, subject to the operational needs of the role - A generous pension scheme, discount portal, cycle to work scheme, access to the University accommodation service, relocation expenses scheme, employee assistance programme and family-friendly policies The funds for this post are available for 3 years in the first instance. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. When applying, please upload your CV and cover letter which clearly sets out how you meet the criteria listed in the person specification (the knowledge, skills, and experience required for the role) along with relevant examples. Candidates will be shortlisted and invited to interview based upon these criteria. Interviews will be held in early November 2026. Additional information regarding the role can be found within the further information file. If you wish to discuss this role in more detail, or have questions about the application process, enquiries are welcome. Please contact the team via change@admin.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference YV51214 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Senior Investment Analyst Key information Department/location University Change Support Office Salary £63,606-£67,468 Reference YV51214 Category Academic-related Date published 29 September 2026 Closing date 25 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/senior-library-assistant-part-time-ve51342": {
      "title": "Senior Library Assistant (Part Time)",
      "description": "Senior Library Assistant (Part Time) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Senior Library Assistant (Part Time) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Senior Library Assistant (Part Time) Ever wanted to work in an institution that is home to one of the world's great collections of cultural treasures and research materials? Spanning thousands of years of human thought and discovery, Cambridge University Libraries and Archives house unique treasures and research materials made up of nearly ten million books, maps, manuscripts, photographs and priceless objects. The role Join the Casimir Lewy Librarian in supporting the delivery of effective, inclusive and user-centred library services to students, researchers and academics within the Faculty of Philosophy, the Institute for Technology and Humanity, and the wider university. The post is permanent and with part-time hours of 29.2 hours per week or FTE 0.8 which can be worked across 4 or 5 days (Monday-Friday). As Senior Library Assistant you will Assist library users with a broad range of enquiries. Create and maintain online reading lists, including integration with the virtual learning environment. Assist in the purchasing, classification and cataloguing of modern books. Participate in the development and delivery of new student inductions and information literacy training. Manage and develop the library's online presence including its webpages, subject guides and social media. What we are looking for Experience of working in a library or information service. Excellent communication and inter-personal skills. A customer-focused approach and a commitment to delivering high-quality services both in-person and online. Excellent attention to detail and organisational skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a small library team, and on projects taking place across the wider Cambridge University Libraries & Archives network. What we offer Flexible working opportunities. Generous annual leave allowance of 36 days. For new part-time employees, annual leave will be pro rata'd based on days worked. Exceptional parental leave (including maternity, paternity / co-parent, adoption and shared parental leave). Discounts on major retailers. Professional development opportunities such as apprenticeships and access to a variety of training courses. In applications, we advise you to clearly state how your skills or experience meet the criteria listed the Person Specification section of the Further Particulars. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. We particularly welcome applications from women and /or candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our department. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For informal enquiries please contact Jo Harcus, Casimir Lewy Librarian at jmh225@cam.ac.uk or 01223 331889. Application closing date: Sunday 25 October 2026. Interview date: Week commencing 2 November 2026 For further details please refer to the Further Particulars. Please quote reference VE51342 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location University Library Salary £27,319-£31,236 pro rata Reference VE51342 Category Assistant staff Date published 12 October 2026 Closing date 25 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/senior-project-coordinator-fixed-term-minderoo-centre-for-technology-and-democracy-en51314": {
      "title": "Senior Project Coordinator (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Senior Project Coordinator (Fixed Term) - Minderoo Centre for Technology and Democracy | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Senior Project Coordinator (Fixed Term) - Minderoo Centre for Technology and Democracy Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Senior Project Coordinator (Fixed Term) - Minderoo Centre for Technology and Democracy This is a fixed term position with current funding until 30th April 2029, open to internal applicants only. We are looking for an organised and proactive Senior Project Coordinator to join the Minderoo Centre for Technology and Democracy (MCTD). This is an exciting time to join a small and driven team as the Centre enters a new phase, launching new projects and expanding into new areas of work. MCTD is an independent team of academic researchers at the University of Cambridge working to address some of the most pressing challenges relating to the governance of the digital technology ecosystem. MCTD is housed within the University of Cambridge Institute for Sustainability Leadership (CISL), enabling opportunities for collaboration with business leaders, civil society and policymakers on responsible AI deployment and AI governance. The role The Senior Project Coordinator is a key administrative role within the team, helping to ensure the efficient delivery of the Centre's projects. You will work independently and closely with the Centre Director and Programme Managers, maintaining a clear understanding of project timelines and budgets and playing a key role in delivering the Centre's objectives, programmes and events in support of a £3 million donation. Your main duties will include: Project Coordination: Coordinate projects from planning through to delivery, monitoring progress, maintaining project information, analysing data and reporting on outcomes. Project Delivery: Support the delivery of projects, events and workshops, while continually improving processes and systems. Financial Administration: Manage project finances, including budgets, purchase orders, invoices and expenses, ensuring compliance with financial procedures. Line Management / Supervision: Provide coaching, mentoring and supervision to junior team members, and may undertake line management responsibilities. Team Support: Organise meetings, events and logistics, maintain project records, and provide administrative support to project teams and senior colleagues. Marketing and Market Intelligence: Support marketing activities, maintain project communications, and undertake market research to inform business development. Relations and Client Management: Build and maintain effective relationships with clients, partners, suppliers and stakeholders, acting as a key point of contact. We are looking for candidates who are interested in the aims of MCTD and committed to the values that underpin the work of MCTD and CISL. In addition, you should be able to demonstrate the following essential skills and experience: Key skills and experience Experience in an administrative role. Experience using Microsoft Office. Excellent planning and organisational skills. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Demonstrable factual and theoretical knowledge of project administration and coordination The role is based at CISL's office in the Entopia Building, Cambridge, with a mix of home and office working. Occasional travel to similar sites may be required. What you'll receive: 36 days annual leave (inc bank holidays). Working 36.5 hours per week ¿ Hybrid/flexible/part-time working considered Excellent benefits including a generous pension scheme, discount portal, cycle to work scheme, access to the University accommodation service, relocation support, employee assistance programme, family friendly policies along with many more. Extensive development opportunities. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. To find out more on how the University supports equal opportunities please visit https://www.equality.admin.cam.ac.uk/ Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have questions about the role, please do not hesitate to email the Minderoo Centre team at minderoo@cisl.cam.ac.uk or Human Resources team at CISL, at recruitment@cisl.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference EN51314 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Senior Project Coordinator Minderoo Key information Department/location University of Cambridge Institute for Sustainability Leadership Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference EN51314 Category Assistant staff Date published 9 October 2026 Closing date 18 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
