      "title": "Events Coordinator",
      "description": "Events Coordinator | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Events Coordinator Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Events Coordinator Would you enjoy bringing people together from across the University and around the world, and turning plans into well-run events and visits? Join the Global Engagement Office (GEO) as an Events Coordinator and play a key role in delivering a varied programme of meetings, conferences, seminars and visits that support the University's international engagement. About the role The role holder will coordinate events and visits from planning through to delivery, working with GEO colleagues and stakeholders from across the University and beyond. This will include incoming and outgoing visits involving senior University colleagues, as well as visits linked to international and diplomatic engagement. The role holder will organise venues, accommodation, catering, travel arrangements, briefings and budgets, ensuring that the practical details are in place for successful delivery. A key part of the role will be facilitating events in person, acting as a point of contact for colleagues, guests, venues and suppliers, and responding to issues as they arise. The role holder will also develop event plans and schedules, coordinate stakeholder contributions, maintain documentation and shared calendars, support invitations, briefings, communications and publicity, undertake risk assessments, monitor expenditure, and contribute to reporting and analysis. Regular in-person working is an important part of the role, including working with colleagues and preparing for and facilitating events and visits. Some events may take place outside normal working hours, including occasional evenings and weekends, for which time off in lieu will be provided. About you You will have experience in an events role or supporting events, together with project management experience across multiple projects or events. Excellent organisational, communication and interpersonal skills are essential, along with the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines. You will be proactive, use your initiative and sound professional judgement, and know when to follow up to keep activities on track. You will communicate accurately and diplomatically with a wide range of stakeholders. Advanced knowledge of events management would be advantageous. Further information For further details about the role, responsibilities and full person specification, please see the Further Particulars. We encourage early applications, as the vacancy may close before the advertised deadline if a sufficient number of suitable applications are received. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to GlobalEngagement.HR@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference AK51357 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Events Coordinator Further Particulars Key information Department/location Global Engagement Office Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference AK51357 Category Assistant staff Date published 16 October 2026 Closing date 6 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/exams-coordinator-temporary-cover-secondment-ab51272": {
      "title": "Exams Coordinator [Temporary Cover] (Secondment)",
      "description": "Exams Coordinator [Temporary Cover] (Secondment) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Exams Coordinator [Temporary Cover] (Secondment) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Exams Coordinator [Temporary Cover] (Secondment) Fixed-term: 31 July 2028. The Team The Exam Operations Team sit within the Student Administration section of Education Services, supporting the academic purposes of the University, and provides expert administrative support and advice to the University and Colleges relating to operational delivery of exams and reasonable adjustments for undergraduate and taught postgraduate courses. It also manages the administration of mitigating circumstances and allowances for undergraduate and taught postgraduate students. About the Role The role is integral in supporting the delivery of a high quality, efficient and coordinated examination and assessment service that adapts to support the University's commitment to diversification of assessment. Working closely with the Exam Operations Lead, the role holder will support the delivery of digital exam services to all stakeholders including students, colleges and University departments and faculties. The role holder will be key in the development and delivery of necessary changes and improvements to exams and assessment as assessment methods continue to diversify. This role will initially focus on supporting the delivery of closed-book digital invigilated exams via a Digital Assessment Platform with extended support of wider exam delivery. The work involved in this role will be varied, key responsibilities are included in the further particulars document.\nGiven the role requirements, we invite applications from individuals who: are an experienced administrator and IT literate (with competent skills in Microsoft programmes such as Excel and Word); have excellent interpersonal and communication skills; are highly flexible and pro-active in approach; have strong organisational skills and multi-tasking ability; have experience of Digital Assessment, preferably in a higher education or further education environment; are educated to degree level or equivalent relevant experience. In return we would offer you: generous annual leave  41 days (including Bank Holidays); a wide range of competitive benefits including shopping, travelling, and health and wellbeing amongst others; a supportive, inclusive and engaging working environment;. a clear training and guidance plan, with supportive training being delivered by colleagues within the team; regular check in's (weekly) with your Line Manager and an annual review; The Exams team is part of the Student Administration Service within Education Services and exceptionally, you may be required to work on other tasks within Education Services if there is a change in priorities. A hybrid work model is possible at certain times, however, the role requires some days per week in the office (exact days to be negotiated). During peak examination times, the role holder will need to be in the office full-time which also includes some Saturday and Bank Holiday working. Interviews will be held in person on Wednesday 2 December in the Student Services Centre. Further information is available via the link below.\n When applying please upload your CV and a covering letter outlining your suitability for the role and how you meet the essential criteria set out in the Person Specification in the Further Particulars. If you would like more information about the role, informal enquiries can be directed by email to Emily.King@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference AB51272 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society.\nThe University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Reference: AB51272 Closing Date: Sunday 15 November 2026 Interview Date: Wednesday 4 December 2026 Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact SSCjobs@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference AB51272 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Student Administration Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference AB51272 Category Academic-related Date published 16 October 2026 Closing date 15 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/head-of-alumni-programming-6-month-cover-dh51391": {
      "title": "Head of Alumni Programming (6-month cover)",
      "description": "Head of Alumni Programming (6-month cover) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Head of Alumni Programming (6-month cover) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Head of Alumni Programming (6-month cover) Lead a team. Influence strategy. Connect a global community. With more than 340,000 alumni worldwide, the University of Cambridge has an extraordinary network of people whose experiences, achievements and connections span almost every sector and corner of the world. We are looking for an experienced leader to join us as Head of Alumni Programming on a six-month secondment, taking responsibility for the team that develops and delivers our global alumni engagement programme. This is an opportunity to combine people leadership, strategic planning and creative programme development, working with colleagues across the University to strengthen lifelong relationships with our alumni. This secondment offers an opportunity to gain experience in the role while recruitment for the permanent position takes place. It may particularly appeal to those interested in exploring the role as a longer-term career opportunity, although appointment to the permanent position would be subject to a separate recruitment process. There may also be scope to extend the secondment should the permanent recruitment process take longer than anticipated, subject to the necessary approvals. The role Reporting to the Director of Alumni Engagement and joining our Extended Leadership Team, you will provide leadership and support to the Alumni Programming team, ensuring colleagues have the clarity and confidence to do their best work. You will take responsibility for the management and performance of the team, its activities and resources, while helping to shape a coordinated, audience-focused approach to alumni communications and engagement. Your responsibilities will include: Managing and motivating the team, setting clear objectives, supporting professional development, managing performance and creating a positive, accountable and collaborative working environment. Leading the Alumni Programming team to deliver an portfolio of alumni events and content, ensuring high-quality, audience-focused engagement across multiple channels. Building on existing audience insights and segmentation approaches, use data analysis to continually enhance content and programming that reflects alumni interests and encourages advocacy, volunteering and philanthropy. Managing budgets, priorities and resources, ensuring complex programmes are delivered effectively and colleagues across different teams work together successfully. You will also represent Alumni Engagement at relevant meetings and events, with occasional UK and international travel. About you You will be an experienced people manager who can provide clear direction, support colleagues and deliver results from the outset. You will bring experience of leading alumni, membership or comparable audience engagement programmes, alongside strong strategic planning, communications and operational management skills. You will be confident managing complex projects, working with senior stakeholders and using data to inform decisions and improve performance. You will understand the importance of building lasting relationships and be comfortable balancing competing priorities while maintaining high standards of delivery. We welcome applications from individuals whose relevant experience has been gained across different sectors, including higher education, membership organisations, charities and commercial environments. What matters is your ability to apply that experience effectively in this role. You will join a welcoming, knowledgeable and committed team where collaboration matters, individual contributions are valued and there is a shared ambition to deliver excellent work. If you are an experienced leader who enjoys developing people, building relationships and making a meaningful contribution, we would be delighted to hear from you. University Development and Alumni Relations - Do your best work here. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. The closing date for this position is midnight on the 29th of October 2026. Interviews for this position are anticipated to take place in the week commencing 9th of November. Please quote reference DH51391 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Candidate Pack - Head of Alumni Programming (6-month cover) Key information Department/location University of Cambridge Development and Alumni Relations Salary £63,606-£67,468 Reference DH51391 Category Academic-related Date published 15 October 2026 Closing date 29 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/hr-adviser-fixed-term-ve51360": {
      "title": "HR Adviser (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "HR Adviser (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs HR Adviser (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs HR Adviser (Fixed Term) We are looking for an experienced HR Professional to join Cambridge University Libraries and Archives HR Team, as our HR Adviser. This is a key role within the HR Team, providing expert advice and coaching to a range of colleagues across the Institution. The role As HR Adviser, you will take the lead on a varied range of employee relations matters. You will work closely with the HR Business Partner and HR Manager, and work in partnership with managers across CULA. You will provide expert advice, build confidence and capability, and help ensure fair, consistent and effective people management. The post is fixed term for 18 months. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. As HR Adviser you will Lead on employee relations matters, including performance management, Dignity at Work, grievance, conduct and sickness absence management. Provide expert, pragmatic advice to managers on employment law and University policies, supporting fair and consistent decision-making. Coach managers through complex people issues, building their confidence and skills to manage cases effectively. Contribute to the design and delivery of management briefings and development sessions across CULA. Work closely with the HR Manager, matrix-manage the HR Coordinator and use workforce data and insights from the wider HR team to identify trends and opportunities for improvement. What we are looking for Strong experience of advising on and managing a broad range of employee relations cases. Sound knowledge of UK employment law and the ability to interpret and apply organisational policies in practice. Excellent coaching, influencing and relationship-building skills, with the confidence to constructively challenge and support managers. Clear and engaging communication skills, including the ability to design and deliver briefings or development sessions. What we offer Flexible and hybrid working opportunities such as part-time hours, and compressed working patterns. Generous annual leave allowance of 41 days. Exceptional parental leave (including maternity, paternity / co-parent, adoption and shared parental leave). Discounts on major retailers. Professional development opportunities such as apprenticeships and access to a variety of training courses. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. We particularly welcome applications from candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our department. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For informal enquiries please contact Natalie Deighton, HR Business Partner, nad50@cam.ac.uk Application closing date: Thursday 29 October 2026 . Interviews date: Wednesday 11 and Thursday 12 November 2026 For further details please refer to the Further Particulars. Please quote reference VE51360 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location University Library Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference VE51360 Category Academic-related Date published 15 October 2026 Closing date 29 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/hr-case-management-coordinator-temporary-cover-ah50896": {
      "title": "HR Case Management Coordinator [Temporary Cover]",
      "description": "HR Case Management Coordinator [Temporary Cover] | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs HR Case Management Coordinator [Temporary Cover] Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs HR Case Management Coordinator [Temporary Cover] The University of Cambridge is recognised globally as a renowned centre for research, education and scholarship. We employ more than 12,500 staff in a range of academic, research and professional services roles, all of whom play a key role in maintaining and enhancing our world leading reputation. Our people are our greatest asset, and it is critical to our continued success that we create the right conditions for our people to thrive at Cambridge. The Case Management team are responsible for the management of formal employee relations cases in one of the largest and most prestigious universities in the UK. We encourage early applications as they will be reviewed on a rolling basis. The vacancy may close before the advertised deadline if a sufficient number of suitable applications are received. Temporary cover: This post is fixed-term for 12 months or the return of the post holder, whichever is the earlier. The Role This is an exciting opportunity to join a new team and the HR Case Management Coordinator will be a key role, leading on the effective coordination of complex and sensitive case management processes. This will include taking minutes, arranging meetings and preparing standard correspondence. The role will also manage and advise on low level case work. About You In order to succeed in this role, you will have: Relevant administrative experience Experience with taking accurate minutes, arranging meetings and maintaining databases Be able to manage confidential information sensitively Excellent interpersonal skills Excellent attention to detail Be able to coordinate work and prioritise your own workload Please note that in addition to the base salary stated above, the successful candidate for this post will receive an additional 2.5% supplement to their pay. Why join us? Competitive rates of pay with automatic service related pay progression and annual cost of living increases; Generous annual leave allowance of 36 days paid leave (including bank holidays); Flexible and hybrid working opportunities; Generous maternity, adoption and shared parental leave entitlement and other family friendly schemes (e.g. workplace nurseries and salary exchange schemes for childcare); An auto-enrolment pension scheme, with a generous employer contribution; Travel benefits and retail discounts at over 2,000 local and national stores; Schemes to support with relocation/the provision of accommodation. The University of Cambridge is committed to supporting our staff to thrive both professionally and personally. We aim to support a good work/life balance, whilst retaining the positive aspects of our unique in-person environment and culture. Elements of this role are suitable for hybrid working, where staff can split their time between in-person collaboration and remote working. The frequency of the remote elements of the role can be discussed with the recruiting manager. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for flexible working arrangements. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. How to Apply For this role, all applications will be managed by Spirehouse Recruitment. To apply, please send your CV to cambridge@spirehouse.co.uk For further information about the role, please contact Abbie Carr (Executive Consultant), abbie@spirehouse.co.uk Closing date: Tuesday 27 October 2026 Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. Download further information HR Case Management Coordinator - Further Information Document Key information Department/location Human Resources Division Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference AH50896 Category Assistant staff Date published 13 October 2026 Closing date 27 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/hr-coordinator-su51400": {
      "title": "HR Coordinator",
      "description": "HR Coordinator | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs HR Coordinator Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs HR Coordinator We are looking to appoint an enthusiastic HR Coordinator, who will be part of a wider integrated professional services team supporting both the Cambridge Mind and Brain Institute (CMBI) and Department of Psychiatry, reporting to the Senior HR Coordinator.\nBased within the CMBI at Chaucer Road, the role will focus on co-ordinating a comprehensive HR and payroll support service for all staff to support the effective operation of the institute. We are looking for a positive and proactive HR Coordinator to join our supportive administration team. This is a fantastic opportunity where your work will directly support the development of cutting-edge research and postgraduate education. If you thrive in a fast-paced environment, enjoy variety in your day-to-day tasks, and are passionate about people and processes, we would love to hear from you.\nYou will be the first point of contact for all HR matters in the Institute and provide advice and guidance to staff.\nThe ideal candidate will be experienced in HR in a coordinator role, have excellent communication skills, the ability to work autonomously and a strong work ethic as well as the ability and motivation to learn new skills and keep abreast of new policy and regulatory changes. Key responsibilities include: -Taking the lead on recruitment and visa matters. -Providing clear and accurate advice to staff on HR policy and employment relations issues. -Providing a helpful and accurate service regarding contractual changes, payroll changes and relevant HR reports. -Coordinating a variety of regular annual schemes, such as reward, appraisal and the HR elements of the Summer Research Placement Schemes. -Providing assistance with PGR matters where necessary. For the full range of responsibilities in this varied role, please refer to the linked Further Particulars document. For more information, email Simon Gurry, Senior HR Coordinator at sjg232@medschl.cam.ac.uk . The closing date for applications is midnight on 6th November 2026 with interview TBC. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role on the online application form. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference SU51400 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location MRC Cognition and Brain Sciences Unit Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference SU51400 Category Assistant staff Date published 14 October 2026 Closing date 6 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/hr-manager-secondment-cover-internal-applicants-only-nm51365": {
      "title": "HR Manager [Secondment Cover] (Internal Applicants Only)",
      "description": "HR Manager [Secondment Cover] (Internal Applicants Only) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs HR Manager [Secondment Cover] (Internal Applicants Only) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs HR Manager [Secondment Cover] (Internal Applicants Only) We have an exciting opportunity for an experienced HR Manager to join our HR team within the Department of Engineering on a temporary basis. The role will provide temporary support to cover a secondment until 31 August 2027. The team is evolving and this role will offer the opportunity to help shape the future of the team and ways of working to ensure a continued high quality service to our colleagues across the department. The Department of Engineering is the largest within the University of Cambridge (approx. 800 staff), and the role holder will play a central part in ensuring the delivery of a high quality, effective HR service within a complex and fast paced environment. We are seeking an experienced HR professional, who will provide advice and guidance to staff and managers, coach and develop their team, and liaise with central HR colleagues to ensure consistent delivery. As part of a collaborative HR team, this role will report into the Departmental Head of HR and work in partnership with another HR Manager to lead a local operational team of HR Coordinators & Administrators to provide a trusted and proactive HR service that delivers operational effectiveness and cultivates a culture of continuous improvement. The team is responsible for the administration across the full employee lifecycle and providing a full generalist HR service within the department, including but not limited to supporting recruitment, probation, managing sickness absence, processing cyclical projects such as reward and promotional schemes and staff reviews, as well as proving advice and guidance on non-complex employee relations matters. The HR Manager will have strong HR advisory experience, excellent UK employment law knowledge and the ability to effectively build strong working relationships. The role holder will be confident and comfortable advising senior colleagues, navigating ambiguity and offering constructive challenge and solutions in line with best practice and University policy and procedure, in order to provide a comprehensive HR support service for staff within the Department. As a HR Manager, you will be expected to support team members learning and development and contribute to a culture of continuous improvement to ensure our processes, documentation and ways of working are both effective and efficient. The department offers a welcoming and inclusive environment, and the opportunity to work alongside supportive and collaborative colleagues. For more information about the department, please visit https://www.eng.cam.ac.uk/ Benefits: 41 days' annual leave (inclusive of bank holidays and University closure days) Generous defined benefit pension scheme Enhanced family leave and pay policies Hybrid and flexible working arrangements Access to a comprehensive wellbeing programme, including EAP, Occupational Health & Staff Counselling Professional networking and access to Personal & Professional Development team Access to recognition and progression schemes Staff discount schemes This is a post to provide secondment cover and will be fixed-term until 31 August 2027 or the return of the post holder, whichever is sooner. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. Interviews will be conducted on Thursday 5 November 2026. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any questions about this vacancy or the application process, please contact the HR Office at the Department of Engineering ( hr-office@eng.cam.ac.uk , 01223 332615). Informal enquiries should be directed to Hannah Archer (Departmental Head of HR) via email: Hannah.Archer@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference NM51365 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Engineering Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference NM51365 Category Academic-related Date published 15 October 2026 Closing date 29 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/hr-reporting-and-information-analyst-fixed-term-ah51361": {
      "title": "HR Reporting and Information Analyst (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "HR Reporting and Information Analyst (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs HR Reporting and Information Analyst (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs HR Reporting and Information Analyst (Fixed Term) The University of Cambridge is recognised globally as a renowned centre for research, education and scholarship. We employ more than 13,000 staff in a range of academic, research and professional services roles, all of whom play a key role in maintaining and enhancing our world leading reputation. Our people are our greatest asset, and it is critical to our continued success that we create the right conditions for our people to thrive at Cambridge. The HR Reporting and Information Analysts will join our HR Analytics team to deliver management information and analysis from the University's HR information systems to senior managers, departments, and other consumers of information across the University. This will include statutory reports, as well as reports for committees and departments and ad hoc analysis to support change initiatives. The primary focus of this role will be to support preparation for the REF (Research Excellence Framework) and will have dotted reporting line to the Principal Research Information Analyst in the Research Office. The role will also support other data and digital services across the research cycle. We welcome applications from employees who have completed the Level 4 Data Analyst Fellowship. The Role: As the HR Reporting and Information Analyst at Cambridge you will be: Gathering and documenting requirements from end users of reports. Developing new reports and dynamic data visualisations using tool such as Power BI, Cognos, MS Fabric, Excel etc, formatting output so it's suitable for nonspecialist audience. Specifying new data extracts from live systems and working with University Information Services (UIS) staff to deliver the new extracts ensuring that the data is valid and credible. With other members of the team, as necessary, delivers information to precise quality standards and to tight schedules in order to satisfy the requirements of the REF and  statutory returns, e.g. Higher Education Statistics Agency (HESA) staff return, Freedom of Information Act requests etc About you: In order to succeed in this role, you will join us with: A customer focused approach to service delivery Advanced data manipulation and analytical skills, ideally in a Microsoft environment Experience of using a reporting tools for reporting from enterprise systems Analytical and problem-solving skills such as when experiencing difficulty in finding the best technical approach to a report. Further information about the role and its responsibilities is available via the link below. Benefits of working at Cambridge include: Competitive rates of pay with automatic service related pay progression and annual cost of living increases; Generous annual leave allowance of 41 days paid leave (including bank holidays) Flexible and hybrid working opportunities; An auto-enrolment pension scheme , with a generous employer contribution; The University of Cambridge is committed to supporting our staff to thrive both professionally and personally. We aim to support a good work/life balance, whilst retaining the positive aspects of our unique in-person environment and culture. Elements of this role are suitable for hybrid working, where staff can split their time between in-person collaboration and remote working. The frequency of the remote elements of the role can be discussed with the recruiting manager. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 18 months in the first instance. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Closing date for applications: Midnight, Sunday 1st November 2026 Interviews for the role will be held: Week commencing 16th November 2026 Please quote reference AH51361 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Human Resources Division Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference AH51361 Category Academic-related Date published 13 October 2026 Closing date 1 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/innovation-engagement-manager-lp51341": {
      "title": "Innovation Engagement Manager",
      "description": "Innovation Engagement Manager | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Innovation Engagement Manager Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Innovation Engagement Manager Are you passionate about turning groundbreaking ideas into meaningful action? Do you thrive at the intersection of innovation, entrepreneurship, research and partnership-building? If so, this is an exciting opportunity to join Cambridge Zero and play a pivotal role in driving climate innovation. The Role We are seeking an enthusiastic and highly organised Innovation Engagement Manager to play a central role in delivering Cambridge Zero's innovation programme. This is an exciting opportunity to support the development and scale-up of climate and nature innovations emerging from across the University, working at the interface of research, entrepreneurship, industry and impact. As a key member of the Cambridge Zero Innovation team, the postholder will work closely with the Head of Innovation to deliver an ambitious portfolio of innovation and entrepreneurship activities. The successful candidate will ensure projects, programmes and partnerships are developed and delivered effectively, efficiently and to a high standard, helping maximise the real-world impact of climate and sustainability innovation. The successful candidate will be a proactive and collaborative individual with experience in innovation, entrepreneurship, knowledge exchange or programme management. You will have excellent organisational and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects and build productive relationships across diverse communities. You will be passionate about accelerating climate and nature innovation and motivated by the opportunity to help translate cutting-edge research into solutions that address global sustainability challenges. About Cambridge Zero Cambridge Zero exists to maximise the University of Cambridge's contribution towards achieving a resilient and sustainable world. We do this by enabling, integrating and accelerating climate activities related to education, research, policy and innovation. We work in a co-ordinating and supporting role across the full academic lifecycle; connecting, convening and engaging the full breadth of the greater University community (i.e. the University, Colleges and related institutions). Acting in close collaboration and partnership with a broad range of University functions, we help integrate, enhance and accelerate climate activities. The deadline for applications is midnight on 15th November 2026 Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. We particularly welcome applications from women and /or candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our department/institution/Faculty/School/University. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please upload your CV and Cover letter to the application. Please note that additional uploaded documents will not be considered as part of recruitment. You should clearly set out how you meet the criteria listed in the person specification (the skills and experience required for the role) along with relevant examples. Candidates will be shortlisted based on these criteria. Deadline for applications: 15th November 2026 Interviews w/c 30th November 2026 For informal enquiries regarding this position, please contact Nina Martin, Operations Manager ( nina.martin@admin.cam.ac.uk ) Please quote reference LP51341 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Document Key information Department/location Cambridge Zero Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference LP51341 Category Academic-related Date published 13 October 2026 Closing date 15 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/junior-clinical-training-scholarship-internship-in-small-animal-neurology-pp51407": {
      "title": "Junior Clinical Training Scholarship (Internship) in Small Animal Neurology",
      "description": "Junior Clinical Training Scholarship (Internship) in Small Animal Neurology | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Junior Clinical Training Scholarship (Internship) in Small Animal Neurology Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Junior Clinical Training Scholarship (Internship) in Small Animal Neurology FUNDED BY THE UNIVERSITY OF CAMBRIDGE VETERINARY SCHOOL TRUST, EXEMPT CHARITY XO 979/86 SCHOLARSHIP AWARD: £23,068.50 (TAX EXEMPT) per annum. \nOn site accommodation is available for £300 per month including bills. Duration of scholarship: 12 months The Department seeks to recruit a Junior Clinical Training Scholar (JCTS) in Small Animal Neurology from January 2027, or as soon as possible after that date, in order to enhance provision of the Small Animal Neurology service and undergraduate teaching. You will help to facilitate the smooth running of the Small Animal Neurology service by supporting the team with all aspects of the work-up, diagnosis and management of small animal surgical patients, helping with scheduling of appointments, preparation for and assisting with surgeries, and the post-surgical aftercare and discharge of the patients. You will contribute to the ongoing clinical research conducted within the Neurology department. You will support final-year veterinary students during their small animal neurology rotation. The successful candidate will be involved in all aspects of the Small Animal Neurology Service and will be required to participate in the practical instruction of veterinary students and a weekend / weeknight on call rota within the Hospital. This is an opportunity to develop your clinical and organisational skills, knowledge of small animal neurology, and to gain experience as a clinical teacher of final year veterinary students in a well-equipped and encouraging academic environment. The Internship will offer an excellent opportunity to prepare for Specialist training, such as a Senior Clinical Training Scholarship (Residency) in Small Animal Neurology. Candidates must be members of the RCVS and have at least 12 months' experience in companion animal practice. Candidates with some pre-existing experience in small animal neurology or who have completed a rotating Small Animal Internship will be preferred. We would welcome anyone wishing to apply for this scholarship to arrange a visit to the hospital to meet the team and find out more. To arrange a visit to the hospital and for informal enquiries about the scholarship programme, please contact Paul Freeman, Principal Clinical Neurologist, by email: pf266@cam.ac.uk . Summary of benefits: Competitive tax-free stipend with heavily subsidized accommodation and bills in Central Cambridge Good work-life balance with manageable weekend and night work University library and journal access 2 weeks of elective/dedicated research time on top of holidays Academic opportunities, e.g. teaching Cambridge students during rotations and College supervision opportunities; weekly department research and clinical seminars; journal and book clubs Proven track-record with publications and research projects with guidance on presentation and scientific writing skills. Assigned intern supervisor: - regular progress meetings, interview practice, provision of professional references and CV/cover letter proof reading by experienced senior clinicians to aid residency applications Generous CPD allowance and encouragement to present at scientific meetings An application form (JCTS1) and information pack can be downloaded from the link below or via the following website: http://www.vet.cam.ac.uk/job Applicants should supply a completed Junior Clinical Training Scholarship Application Form (JCTS 1), a CV and Covering Letter giving reasons for wishing to undertake the JCTS in the Department of Veterinary Medicine, University of Cambridge. Applications should be submitted via e-mail to: vetmed@vet.cam.ac.uk with the above documents as one attachment, by the closing date stated. For more information about the Department and the role please visit: www.vet.cam.ac.uk Please note:\nThe ability to take up this Scholarship is contingent upon you being able to evidence your right to work in the UK, or through gaining the right to work via the UK immigration system. Evidence will need to be provided before an offer can be made. Regrettably, this Scholarship is not suitable for sponsorship via the Skilled Worker or Temporary Worker visa routes as the minimum requirements cannot be met. Other visa options may be available depending on your individual circumstances. Further information can be found on the UK Government website: https://www.gov.uk/browse/visas-immigration/work-visas . All visa related costs are the responsibility of the applicant. These charges will not be reimbursed by the University, regardless of the outcome of the application. Please quote reference PP51407 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Download further information APPLICATION FORM (JCTS 1) - JCTS in Small Animal Neurology (Funded by Camvet) INFORMATION PACK - JCTS (Internship) in Small Animal Neurology (Funded by Camvet) Key information Department/location Department of Veterinary Medicine Salary Reference PP51407 Category Studentships Date published 15 October 2026 Closing date 28 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/mphil-programme-administrator-ns51387": {
      "title": "MPhil Programme Administrator",
      "description": "MPhil Programme Administrator | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs MPhil Programme Administrator Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs MPhil Programme Administrator Cambridge Judge Business School (CJBS) leverages the power of academia for real-world impact to transform individuals, organisations, and society. Since 1990, Cambridge Judge has forged a reputation as a centre of rigorous thinking and high-impact transformative education, situated within one of the world's most prestigious universities. This role sits within the MPhil Programmes Office at Cambridge Judge Business School (CJBS). The purpose of the role is to ensure compliance with overarching university teaching and examination policies and procedures. Specifically, this MPhil Programme Administrator will be responsible for the day-to-day administration, assessment and examinations for  the MPhil in Management programme. The MPhil Programme Administrator reports directly to the Head of Programmes Office and will also have regular contact with the MPhil in Management Programme Director and the Chair of Examiners. The role holder also works closely with other MPhil Programme Administrators and Programme Directors, with peers from other CJBS departments, with Colleges and with other central University departments. Why work for Cambridge Judge Business School? We are the business school of the University of Cambridge, advancing knowledge and leadership through people who leave a mark on the world.  Cambridge Judge Business School leverages the power of academia for real world impact to transform individuals, organisations and society. Since 1990, we have forged a reputation as a centre of rigorous thinking and high-impact transformative education, situated within one of the world's most prestigious research universities, and in the heart of the Cambridge Cluster, the most successful technology entrepreneurship cluster in Europe. Benefits of working for Cambridge Judge Business School: You'll receive excellent benefits at Cambridge Judge Business School including: Generous holiday allowance Defined benefits pension schemes Flexible working options Family-friendly initiatives Career development opportunities Support for health and mental wellbeing Discounts on shopping Tax-efficient bicycle and charity-giving schemes More information is available on our website - Staff benefits - Jobs at Cambridge Judge Business School - Cambridge Judge Business School Application process: To view more details about the role and person specification, please click the Further Information link. Closing Date: 27 October 2026 Interview Dates: TBD If you have any queries regarding the application process, please contact: hrsupport@jbs.cam.ac.uk Additional Information: The University is supportive of hybrid working, where some work is undertaken on University premises and some in a remote working environment. The aim of our approach is to enable as many staff as possible to work in a hybrid way if they wish and where their role allows ¿ we expect most colleagues to spend at least 50% of their time at their dedicated office location. This arrangement is subject to change and will not form a part of the contractual terms of the role. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role on the online application form. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference NS51387 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Judge Business School Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference NS51387 Category Assistant staff Date published 13 October 2026 Closing date 27 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/pathways-to-inclusive-practice-in-clinical-medicine-project-manager-fixed-term-ra51388": {
      "title": "Pathways to Inclusive Practice in Clinical Medicine Project Manager (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Pathways to Inclusive Practice in Clinical Medicine Project Manager (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Pathways to Inclusive Practice in Clinical Medicine Project Manager (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Pathways to Inclusive Practice in Clinical Medicine Project Manager (Fixed Term) Would you like to help change how future doctors with a disability or neurodivergent diagnosis are supported? The School of Clinical Medicine is looking for a Project Manager to run the clinical medicine part of the Pathways to Inclusive Practice pilot. This is a new approach to supporting students in the final years of their medical training. The role is varied. You'll manage the project day to day, including plans, budgets and risks, and be its main contact for students, University and NHS staff, and external partners. You'll also analyse focus group data and build a project database in Power BI with an AI search interface. You'll then train staff to use it. We're looking for someone with: Experience in project or administrative roles, ideally including work with students Strong organisational, communication and analytical skills An understanding of disability and neurodiversity, from professional or lived experience Confidence with Microsoft 365, plus some experience of Power BI or similar tools A degree, a Level 6 vocational qualification, or equivalent practical experience For the full range of responsibilities in this varied role, please refer to the linked Further Particulars document. The closing date for applications is midnight on 4th November 2026 with interview 16th November 2026 Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 12 months in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role on the online application form. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference RA51388 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars (RA51388) Key information Department/location Office of the School of Clinical Medicine Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference RA51388 Category Assistant staff Date published 13 October 2026 Closing date 4 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
