ecruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs PhD Studentships in Institute for Energy and Environmental Flows  (Fixed Term) We are delighted to announce a series of PhD Scholarships for students with backgrounds in Applied Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry, Earth Sciences, Chemical Engineering or Engineering, interested in embarking on a PhD project related to energy, environment and fluid mechanics, in the Institute. Details of the research in the Institute may be found here ( https://ieef.cam.ac.uk/research/ ) and some of the possible PhD projects related to this scheme are listed here ( https://ieef.cam.ac.uk/new-phd-scholarships-available/ ) Applications should be made through the University Application system, listing the preferred project and indicating that the research will be carried out in the Institute. It is recommended that applications should be submitted before 15 December 2026. The PhD Scholarships will fund living expenses and graduate fees at a level comparable to a UKRI home-based PhD studentship for 3.5 years. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 3.5 years in the first instance. For further information please see https://ieef.cam.ac.uk/new-phd-scholarships-available/ Please quote reference LB51220 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Key information Department/location Department of Earth Sciences Salary Reference LB51220 Category Studentships Date published 14 October 2026 Closing date 15 December 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
