    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/programme-manager-fixed-term-en51356": {
      "title": "Programme Manager (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Programme Manager (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Programme Manager (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Programme Manager (Fixed Term) We are looking for an excellent communicator, looking for an opportunity to translate cutting edge research on AI governance and sustainability to shape policy and civil society response within an inspiring, world-leading organisation? Do you want to contribute to our mission to create a more sustainable economy? The Minderoo Centre for Technology and Democracy (MCTD) is an independent team of academic researchers at the University of Cambridge working to address the most pressing challenges to the governance of the digital technology ecosystem. MCTD is housed in the University of Cambridge Institute for Sustainability Leadership (CISL), enabling routes to collaboration with business leaders, civil society and policymakers on responsible AI deployment and AI governance. The role We are looking for two programme managers to join the team. The roles are based in CISL's Cambridge office and provide an opportunity to join a dynamic and fast-paced team that brings academic research to leaders and decisionmakers in business government and civil society to address the most pressing challenges to the governance of the digital technology ecosystem. The roles' responsibilities entail translating research outputs into impact by communicating research to informing decision makers in government, civil society and business; supporting international collaboration and stakeholder engagement in the UK and other jurisdictions about research topics; and leading and convening in broader conversations with leaders in policy, civil society, and industry, in order to build societal capacity for the responsible and sustainable use and governance of AI. One role will focus on building and sustaining stakeholder relationships with the private sector, and the other role will focus on policy impact engagement. However, we expect people in these roles to work closely together, alongside the MCTD Director, to lead MCTD's engagement with civil society, business and policy leaders.  This includes: convening and expanding stakeholder communities for MCTD research to increase research impact; producing policy evidence and public-facing reports for diverse audiences based on MCTD's research, commissioning and editing public-facing reports as appropriate, leading business and programmatic development, supporting communications and relationship management for MCTD development, and managing the effective oversight and evaluation of MCTD's programmes and platforms. Key skills and experience (the full list of key skills is available in the further information pack) Understanding emerging issues around responsible AI, AI and sustainability and AI governance. Understanding of research impact activities including issues of research ethics and integrity. Experience in leading impact and engagement activities or in developing or shaping policy Experience in successfully managing projects which involve multiple clients or stakeholders Experience of working with research experts and on complex multidisciplinary projects Excellent relationship-management skills and a proven ability to build, grow and maintain relationships with collaborators, delivery partners, sponsors and external stakeholders What you'll receive: 41 days annual leave (including. bank holidays). Working 37 hours per week - Hybrid/flexible working considered Excellent benefits including a generous pension scheme, discount portal, cycle to work scheme, access to the University accommodation service, relocation support, employee assistance programme, family friendly policies along with many more. Extensive development opportunities. This post is fixed term, full-time on a hybrid working basis with at least 2 days in our award-winning Cambridge office. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available until 30 April 2029 in the first instance. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. We particularly welcome applications from women and /or candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our department/institution/Faculty/School/University. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any questions about this vacancy please contact CISLHuman.Resources@cisl.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference EN51356 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location University of Cambridge Institute for Sustainability Leadership Salary £42,254-£56,535 Reference EN51356 Category Academic-related Date published 15 October 2026 Closing date 1 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
