    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-assistant-fixed-term-go51405": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Assistant (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant (Fixed Term) The Leverhulme Centre for the Future of Intelligence (CFI), with the Institute for Technology and Humanity (ITH) at the University of Cambridge, is seeking a full-time Research Assistant for 12 months in the first instance to support the CAPAIBLE laboratory - Cognition and Predictability in AI Behaviour: Laboratory for Evaluation. The Research Assistant will join the Kinds of Intelligence team at CFI, a multidisciplinary team comprising expertise in Computer Science, AI, Cognitive Science and related fields. The Department CFI is a highly interdisciplinary research centre addressing the challenges and opportunities posted by artificial intelligence, in both the short and long term. CFI is based at the University of Cambridge, with partners in Imperial College London, and UC Berkeley, and close links with industry and policymakers. More information is available at: https://www.lcfi.ac.uk/ The Role The Research Assistant's main duty will be supporting the day-to-day activities of CAPAIBLE, playing a key role in keeping the laboratory running smoothly and helping the research team focus on its core scientific work. Responsibilities span research coordination, stakeholder engagement, internal communication, and public-facing activities. Strong organisational and interpersonal skills are essential, as the role involves working closely with a diverse, interdisciplinary team and a range of external collaborators and partners. Applicants should have, or be close to obtaining, an undergraduate or postgraduate degree in a relevant discipline. We are looking for someone who is proactive, and comfortable working across a broad range of tasks - from coordinating meetings and managing communications to supporting grant reporting and public engagement. Experience in a research environment is desirable, as is familiarity with AI or cognitive science. All applicants should be able to demonstrate strong motivation in line with the goals of CFI. Further Information Please see the Further Particulars document for more information. In order for your application of be considered, please upload the following: Curriculum Vitae (CV), which should include the names of two referees. A covering letter of no more than 500 words explaining your interest in the position and outlining how you meet the criteria set out in the person specification within the Further Particulars. In the covering letter, you can optionally include a link to a coding project you carried out, and you believe demonstrates your programming ability. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 12 months in the first instance. The closing date for applications is midnight (GMT) on Sunday 1 November 2026. Interviews are planned for mid-November, subject to change. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries about the role are welcomed and should be directed to Professor Jose Hernandez-Orallo at jh2135@cam.ac.uk . For questions on the application process, please contact the School's HR Team on sahhr@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference GO51405 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Cambridge Institute for Technology and Humanity Salary £33,002-£35,608 Reference GO51405 Category Research Date published 15 October 2026 Closing date 1 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-assistant-part-time-fixed-term-rn51389": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Part Time, Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Assistant (Part Time, Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant (Part Time, Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant (Part Time, Fixed Term) This post will be based at the University of Cambridge in the Department of Psychiatry and work as a Pre-doctoral Research Assistant to support three National Institute for Health & Care Research (NIHR) funded projects for 29.6 hours per week until the end of December 2027. It will support 3 projects  WAIT LESS https://arc-eoe.nihr.ac.uk/research-implementation/research-themes/inclusive-involvement-research-mental-health-over-life-0 , the calibration and validation of Artemis A https://arc-eoe.nihr.ac.uk/research-implementation/research-themes/mental-health-and-wellbeing/calibration-and-utility-artemis and the Attend Well Study. WAIT LESS is now progressing on to a feasibility trial of a new digital intervention for young people with depression on the CAMHS waiting list at two NHS trusts. The post will also be joining the validation of the Artemis A computer adaptive testing algorithm against clinical research diagnosis and seeing how profiles change with treatment in clinical samples from various parts of the UK. They will be based in Cambridge but liaise with colleagues at trusts in Norwich, Berkshire, Liverpool, Manchester and London. This list might expand as other partners come on board. The work requires knowledge and experience of psychometrics, analysis of large quantitative datasets, clinical trials and evaluations. The successful applicant will also support the delivery of the Attend Well study, particularly organising and running the Young People's PPI panel, supporting participant recruitment and assisting with data collection and other research activities. We welcome applicants who would like to use this opportunity to develop further research proposals fellowship applications or other grants from the work completed. The Child and Adolescent Resilience and Mental Health Research group undertakes applied epidemiology, as well as intervention development and evaluation. The successful applicant will be at a junior level but will have the opportunity to supporting placement students. We are particularly interested in someone with experience of psychometric analysis and quantitative methods. The methods applied by the team include secondary analysis of large epidemiological datasets, mixed qualitative and quantitative observational studies, economic evaluation systematic reviews, and randomized controlled trials. The research is inherently translational and multi-disciplinary, and involves strong links with psychology, pediatrics, education, epidemiology, trial specialists, statisticians, health economics and basic scientists. Though we are looking for an applicant at a junior level, we envisage that they will eventually become involved in all aspects of this work. Applicants will have a bachelor's degree in psychology psychology, or equivalent, a strong knowledge of assessment and outcome measures in relation to children and young people's mental health. Experience of working with administrative data would be desirable but is not essential.\nFor further details, please read the further particulars, please provide at least 3 references, a CV and covering letter indicating how you meet the criteria for this post. Informal enquiries may be directed to Professor Tamsin Ford via ChARM@medschl.cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact Simon Gurry, HR Coordinator ( hradminpsychiatry@medschl.cam.ac.uk ). Deadline for applications is  27th October 2026, with interviews TBC Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available until 31 December 2027 in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter and a CV in the Upload section of the online application. The covering letter should outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference RN51389 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Psychiatry Salary £33,002-£35,608 pro rata Reference RN51389 Category Research Date published 13 October 2026 Closing date 27 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-assistant-luisi-group-fixed-term-ph51221": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Assistant - Luisi Group (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant - Luisi Group (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant - Luisi Group (Fixed Term) Applications are invited for a fixed-term Research Assistant position in the Department of Biochemistry, University of Cambridge, UK. The successful applicant will work to support the research activities in the laboratory of Professor Ben Luisi, under supervision of Dr Pedro Rebelo-Guiomar, to study the delivery of nucleic acids to mitochondria. The position would suit an ambitious and talented researcher who is keen to gain research experience in an international academic environment. The focus of the post is to assist the development of methods for the delivery of nucleic acids into mitochondria. We are a highly interactive, research-led group, driven to innovate with cutting-edge research and a collaborative environment. In addition to a strong aptitude for scientific research, the ideal candidate should possess excellent communication, organisation and team-work skills. A MSc degree in Biochemistry, Cell Biology, Molecular Biology or adjacent areas, and previous research experience is required for the position. Applicants should submit a cover letter, CV citing relevant experience and contact information of at least two references. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available from 15th January 2027 until 5th December 2027, in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For informal enquiries, please contact Dr Pedro Guiomar via pfrg2@cam.ac.uk . For queries regarding the application process, please contact the Biochemistry HR Team via: personnel@bioc.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference PH51221 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars - Research Assistant (Luisi Group) Key information Department/location Department of Biochemistry Salary £33,002-£35,608 Reference PH51221 Category Research Date published 13 October 2026 Closing date 11 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
