    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-assistant-associate-fixed-term-go51404": {
      "title": "Research Assistant / Associate (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Assistant / Associate (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant / Associate (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant / Associate (Fixed Term) The Leverhulme Centre for the Future of Intelligence (CFI), with the Institute for Technology and Humanity (ITH) at the University of Cambridge invites applications for two Research Assistant / Associates. The appointment will be full-time, for 24 months in the first instance (ideal start date 1st of December, or soon after that). The successful candidates will work on a project focused on establishing \"red lines\" for AI using cognitive capability and propensity profiles. The work will focus on AI Evaluation and will be drawing from multiple disciplines, but primarily from artificial intelligence, technical AI safety, Bayesian statistics and causal modelling, psychology and AI governance. Appointment at the Research Associate level is dependent on the award of a PhD. This is a postdoctoral-level appointment, those who have submitted but not yet received their PhD will be appointed at the Research Assistant -Grade 5, which will be amended to Research Associate-Grade 7 once the award of the PhD has been conferred. CFI is a highly interdisciplinary research centre addressing the challenges and opportunities posed by artificial intelligence (AI). Based at the University of Cambridge, the Centre has close links with industry, policymakers, and many academic disciplines. In order for your application to be considered, please upload the following: Curriculum Vitae (CV) A Covering Letter of no more than 1,000 words. This should detail relevant experience and interests with particular regard to this project The names and contact details of two referees who are familiar with your work. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Informal enquiries about the role are welcomed and should be directed to Professor Jose Hernandez-Orallo at jh2135@cam.ac.uk . For questions on the application process, please contact the School's HR Team on sahhr@admin.cam.ac.uk . The closing date for applications is midnight (GMT) on Sunday 1st of November 2026. Interviews are planned for the second week of November, subject to change. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 2 years in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please quote reference GO51404 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Cambridge Institute for Technology and Humanity Salary £33,002-£46,049 Reference GO51404 Category Research Date published 16 October 2026 Closing date 1 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-assistant-research-associate-fixed-term-rr51415": {
      "title": "Research Assistant / Research Associate (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Assistant / Research Associate (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant / Research Associate (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant / Research Associate (Fixed Term) The Opportunity We are seeking individuals with strong academic background and entrepreneurial ambitions to join our academic lab. You would be joining a team focused on translating novel wearable medical devices from academic prototypes to clinical adoption, with home-based feasibility testing starting in 2027. Our lab is aiming to translate this with a spin-out in the next 24-48 months. These devices focus on measuring various body and eye movement metrics, and pair with rehabilitation apps. Funding has been secured for SENSE Lab to cover a postdoctoral researcher for 12 months, with potential scope for ongoing involvement in a future spin-out company,. Position could be extended dependent on further funding and new project requirements. The work sits at the intersection of algorithm design, human biomechanics, electronic engineering and hardware development, driven strongly by the lab's clinical expertise. Individuals with a multidisciplinary skillset and analytical background would particularly enjoy the role at the cutting edge of academic research and development. We would be interested in applicants with either of the two following profiles: Potential Profile A: Biomechanics, Sensing & Data You may have a background in areas such as: Human biomechanics, movement science or biomedical engineering Inertial measurement units (IMUs) and wearable sensing Experimental data collection Signal processing and sensor-data processing Sensor fusion, algorithm development or validation Potential Profile B: Electronics, Instrumentation & Hardware You may have a background in areas such as: PCB design and prototyping Microcontrollers and embedded programming Electronic and/or material design for biosignal acquisition Hardware integration, testing and validation We are also interested in people who don't fit neatly into either profile, but feel their background is well suited for this. What You Will be Doing Activities may include: Developing algorithms for extracting clinically meaningful metrics from sensor data Building device testing platforms (e.g. web, smartphone or tablet-based apps) Running experiments to collect data and test device usability, informing future design iterations Designing, prototyping and testing electronic hardware Integrating sensors, electronics, firmware and analysis software Ensuring the devices adhere to medical device regulations The precise balance of activities will be shaped by the successful candidate's skills and interests. What You Will Join Successful candidates will work on translating our wearable sensor-based platforms from the lab to clinical adoption. These platforms seek to enhance the treatment of vestibular and balance disorders by providing objective clinical metrics, originating from prior and ongoing research in SENSE Lab. Having established the clinical need and viability, the team's focus has turned towards translating the devices from research prototypes into certified medical devices, ready to enter the market. Having originated as an academic project, the team is looking to translate this in the near future, as a company, and the successful candidate could potentially be directly involved with the transition from the academic domain to a commercial entity. Applications are invited for Positions in an academic-based spinout: Research Assistant / Postdoctoral Research Associate, Wearable Sensing, Biomechanics, Signal Processing & Electronic Hardware. Location: Onsite at Cambridge Biomedical Campus Contract: 1 year full time Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For questions relating to the post, please contact Professor Manohar Bance  at mlb59@cam.ac.uk , or Dr Iwan Roberts at ivr22@cam.ac.uk Appointment at Research Associate level (Grade 7) is dependent upon having been awarded their PhD. Those who have submitted but not yet had their PhD conferred will be appointed as a Research Assistant (Grade 5). Upon award the successful candidate will transfer to a Research Associate position. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter and CV in the Upload section of the online application. The covering letter should outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Closing Date: 1st November 2026 Interview Date: to be confirmed Please quote reference RR51415 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Clinical Neurosciences Salary £34,610 £37,694-£46,049 Reference RR51415 Category Research Date published 15 October 2026 Closing date 1 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-assistantassociate-in-environmental-impacts-of-future-aircraft-fixed-term-nm51382": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Associate in Environmental Impacts of Future Aircraft (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Assistant/Associate in Environmental Impacts of Future Aircraft (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant/Associate in Environmental Impacts of Future Aircraft (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant/Associate in Environmental Impacts of Future Aircraft (Fixed Term) Hydrogen and electric aircraft could transform aviation's climate and air quality footprint, but their environmental impacts remain poorly quantified. \nA position exists, for a Research Assistant/Associate in the Department of Engineering, to work on the Environmental Impacts of Next-Generation Aircraft, developing aircraft emissions and air quality models as part of the EU-funded SESAR project ZENITIA. \nThe post holder will join Dr Irene Dedoussi's group at the Whittle Laboratory and work with project partners including UC3M, Imperial, TU Delft and Boeing. The research will inform airport and air traffic management and European aviation policy. The key responsibilities and duties are: developing global emissions inventories for current and next-generation aircraft under scenarios to 2050, including landing and take-off modelling; developing, evaluating and applying near-airport air quality modelling capabilities; collaborating with consortium partners and contributing to project deliverables; publishing and presenting research results. The skills, qualifications and experience required to perform the role are: has obtained or is close to obtaining a PhD in aerospace, mechanical or chemical engineering, atmospheric or environmental science, physics, applied mathematics or a related field; experience in modelling physical systems (e.g. atmospheric modelling, aircraft performance, propulsion, combustion or fluid dynamics); strong scientific programming skills; a publication record appropriate to career stage and excellent communication skills. Experience in aviation emissions, chemistry transport, dispersion or air quality modelling is desirable. Appointment at Research Associate level is dependent on having a PhD. Those who have submitted but not yet received their PhD will be appointed at Research Assistant level, which will be amended to Research Associate once the PhD has been awarded. Salary Ranges: Research Assistant: £33,002 - £35,608 Research Associate: £37,694 - £46,049 Fixed-term: The funding is for 24 months or until 28 February 2029, whichever of these comes soonest. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload your Curriculum Vitae (CV), including a list of publications, a covering letter, and your most representative research publication in the Upload section of the online application. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please submit your application by midnight on the closing date, although early applications are strongly encouraged. If you have any questions about this vacancy, please contact Dr Irene Dedoussi at icd23@cam.ac.uk for queries of a technical nature related to the role, and Juliet Teather  at jet63@eng.cam.ac.uk for queries related to the application process. Please quote reference NM51382 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information HR7_RA in Environmental Impacts of Next-Generation Aircraft Key information Department/location Department of Engineering Salary £34,610 - £35,608 £37,694 - £46,049 Reference NM51382 Category Research Date published 13 October 2026 Closing date 3 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
