    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/communications-and-community-engagement-manager-fixed-term-xz51468": {
      "title": "Communications and Community Engagement Manager (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Communications and Community Engagement Manager (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Communications and Community Engagement Manager (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Communications and Community Engagement Manager (Fixed Term) The Milner Therapeutics Institute (MTI) is seeking to recruit a Communications and Community Engagement Manager. This is a fantastic opportunity for a motivated individual to join the MTI. The role will deliver strategic communications, marketing, and events for the Institute. The MTI is a unique institute at the University of Cambridge where academics, start-ups and pharma companies work side by side in shared office and laboratory space. The MTI encompasses both a research institute and a global outreach programme, with an overarching mission to transform pioneering science into therapies. The institute connects academia with industry to drive collaborative research and accelerate therapeutic companies. It also has its own research capabilities in human disease modelling, therapeutic target discovery, functional genomics and Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning. As a Communications and Community Engagement Manager, you will have proven experience in communications, data analysis and line management. You will be able to demonstrate a good understanding of using social networking tools as well as strong editorial and writing skills. Ideally, you will be educated to degree level and hold an academic qualification. Before applying, please read the further information document linked below for role responsibilities and person specification. The closing date for the role is 15 November 2026. The interview dates for the role are expected to be 24 and 26 November 2026. The funds for this post are available for 3 years in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please quote reference XZ51468 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information FPs Key information Department/location Milner Therapeutics Institute Salary £47,389-£59,966 Reference XZ51468 Category Academic-related Date published 22 October 2026 Closing date 15 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/data-and-study-coordinator-fixed-term-rh51436": {
      "title": "Data and Study Coordinator (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Data and Study Coordinator (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Data and Study Coordinator (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Data and Study Coordinator (Fixed Term) The Cardiovascular Epidemiology Unit (CEU), directed by Professor John Danesh, is an internationally recognised interdisciplinary group dedicated to understanding and preventing cardiovascular disease. CEU is part of the Department of Public Health and Primary Care (DPHPC), one of Europe's leading centres for population health research. Guided by a commitment to scientific excellence, public benefit, and a supportive research culture, CEU is seeking a dynamic individual to coordinate access to health data and support the management of major population-health cohort studies in the UK and South Asia. Health Data The post-holder will coordinate access to external population-health resources, including UK Biobank, Our Future Health and All of Us. They will also manage the end-to-end process for accessing CEU cohort data, supporting internal and external researchers from application through to secure data access. One aspect of the role will be establishing and maintaining relationships with electronic health record (EHR) data providers and coordinating governance, contractual and operational arrangements to enable secure, high-quality data linkages for CEU's large-scale cohort studies. Cohort Studies The role will also support the coordination of CEU's cohort studies, including BELIEVE, a major global health study of 74,000 participants in Bangladesh. BELIEVE investigates the biological, behavioural, environmental and social determinants of non-communicable diseases through long-term follow-up and multi-omics research. Further information is available at https://www.believestudy-bangladesh.org/ . Our UK Blood Donor Studies includes INTERVAL, COMPARE, STRIDES and SHAPE-Plasma, involving approximately 170,000 participants. Further information is available at https://www.donorhealth-btru.nihr.ac.uk/ . Reporting to the Senior Study Manager and working closely with the Research Programme Manager, the successful candidate will bring strong organisational, communication and research coordination skills, together with an understanding of health data governance and collaborative research. The funds for these posts are available until 31 March 2029. This is a full-time position. Location - Victor Phillip Dahdaleh Heart & Lung Research Institute, Biomedical Campus, Papworth Road, Trumpington, Cambridge CB2 0BD (approx 2 miles south of city centre), next to the Cambridge South Railway station. Informal enquiries can be made to Barbara Graves, Research Programme Manager, via email bg339@medschl.cam.ac.uk Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter and CV in the Upload section of the online application. The covering letter should outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Closing Date: 1st November 2026 Interview Date: week commencing 9th November 2026 Please quote reference RH51436 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Department of Public Health and Primary Care, Cardiovascular Epidemiology Unit Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference RH51436 Category Academic-related Date published 19 October 2026 Closing date 1 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
