    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/data-scientist-nihr-bioresource-fixed-term-rw51514": {
      "title": "Data Scientist NIHR BioResource (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Data Scientist NIHR BioResource (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Data Scientist NIHR BioResource (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Data Scientist NIHR BioResource (Fixed Term) Do you have great skills and experience organizing and managing data? Interested in a role \ncontributing to improve lives? Looking for your next challenge? We are recruiting a Data Scientist to provide data to researchers in academia and industry, through cohort discovery by mining phenotypic and genomic data, and to manage metadata assets of the NIHR BioResource projects under the guidance of the line manager. To succeed in this role, you will need to be experienced in the manipulation of big and/or genomics data, the analysis and integration of different data types and the use of meta-data standards and vocabularies. About NIHR BioResource: Our mission is to facilitate human health research and its transformation into medical practice. NIHR BioResource is a unique and powerful resource for studying disease mechanisms and for investigating the links between genes, the environment, health and disease, enabling scientific discoveries as well as facilitating translational medicine for the benefit of patients. Further details on the NIHR BioResource, including some of our COVID-19 research studies, can be found on our website https://bioresource.nihr.ac.uk . About the job: You will be responsible for: Linking of omics data (especially genomics) and biomedical, demographic, and phenotypic data that form a major part of NIHR BioResource data assets to enable participant selection for proposed research studies Contribute to more complex linkage experiments, e.g. where omics data is joined to sample holdings and rich clinical phenotype Prepare datasets for recall-based research studies identifying potential volunteers Prepare de-identified datasets for release to researchers Discussions with researchers re expected standards on data protection, anonymisation and security About you: Ideally you will have: Experience and in-depth knowledge of phenotypic and genomic data and database modelling with proficiency in MySQL and No-SQL or equivalent Proven programming ability in Python is a must with experience in using libraries (such as Pandas and Numpy) Good knowledge of Linux and shell scripting Ability to prioritise and plan work efficiently and meet deadlines and work unsupervised What we offer: The University offers a wide range of benefits including flexible working, family friendly policies, an attractive pension scheme (employer's contribution is 14.5%). and 41 days' annual holiday (inclusive of public holidays). We encourage career development by providing extensive training & development opportunities. This appointment is full-time, 37 hours per week; part-time to 80% will be considered. Work / life balance is important, and we are open to discussion on flexible working, including hybrid working. The post is available on a fixed-term basis until 31 March 2028 in the first instance. NIHR BioResource is funded by the National Institute for Health & Care Research (NIHR) on a 4-year funding cycle. Our offices are on the Cambridge Biomedical Campus CB2 0QQ (approximately 2 miles south of the city centre). See the Further Information link below for full details and Person Specification. This appointment requires a Research Passport application. We encourage informal queries about the job or the application process - please contact Stephane Ballereau,\n Lead Bioinformatician, Stephane.Ballereau@bioresource.nihr.ac.uk . Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter and CV in the Upload section of the online application. The covering letter should outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference RW51514 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars (RW51514) Key information Department/location Department of Haematology, NIHR BioResource Research Group Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference RW51514 Category Academic-related Date published 27 October 2026 Closing date 18 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/deputy-faculty-manager-finance-research-facilities-management-jk51414": {
      "title": "Deputy Faculty Manager",
      "description": "Deputy Faculty Manager - Finance, Research & Facilities Management | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Deputy Faculty Manager - Finance, Research & Facilities Management Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Deputy Faculty Manager - Finance, Research & Facilities Management The Faculty of Law is a world-leading institution for legal research and teaching. We are seeking to appoint a Deputy Faculty Manager with responsibility for finance, research operations and facilities management. This is a key member of the professional services team within a large and busy Faculty. The role holder manages the Faculty's professional services team falling within these areas and is one of two Deputy Faculty Managers (the other role has responsibility or learning & teaching matters) reporting to the Faculty Manager. Key responsibilities: Manage and lead the Faculty's professional services team across finance, research and facilities management, including direct line management responsibilities. Lead on Faculty financial management, including advising the Faculty Officers on the implementation of the Finance Transformation Programme, budget planning, financial forecasting, post costings, trust fund oversight, donation agreements and audit coordination. Monitor income and expenditure, identify financial risks and opportunities, and provide advice to budget holders and senior colleagues. Lead Faculty research operations, including support for research grants, REF-related activities, supporting with Faculty research strategy, liaising with Faculty's research centres and working with the HR team in relation to Faculty research appointments. Oversee facilities management in the building, including room bookings, space allocation, visitor arrangements, building management and projects, health and safety, fire safety and emergency planning. Deliver and support key projects and continuous improvement initiatives across the Faculty. Attend the weekly Faculty Officer (Senior Leadership Team) meetings. Deputise for the Faculty Manager when required, working alongside the other Deputy Faculty Manager. Undertake the roles of Faculty Safety Officer and Fire Officer as part of remit. About you: You will have previous experience of a senior administrative role and of managing a team of staff. The role holder works with staff at all levels so excellent communication skills and interpersonal skills are essential, as is the ability to prioritise and plan effectively. You will have excellent attention to detail and high standards of accuracy. A proactive, positive and flexible approach and ability to use your own initiative are also crucial. \nYou will need the ability to prepare budgets and to manage effectively finances and resources. You should be educated to degree level or have equivalent experience. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any queries regarding the role or the application process, please contact: hr@law.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference JK51414 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Faculty of Law Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference JK51414 Category Academic-related Date published 19 October 2026 Closing date 15 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/deputy-faculty-manager-temporary-cover-ak51396": {
      "title": "Deputy Faculty Manager [Temporary Cover]",
      "description": "Deputy Faculty Manager [Temporary Cover] | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Deputy Faculty Manager [Temporary Cover] Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Deputy Faculty Manager [Temporary Cover] Applications are invited for the fixed-term (maternity cover) post of Deputy Faculty Manager (Teaching and Facilities), a role based in the University's Unified Administrative Service and assigned to the Faculty of History. The Role The role holder will be responsible for the administrative processes underpinning the delivery and examining of the Faculty's undergraduate teaching programmes, and will have an oversight of facilities work and resource issues relating to teaching. This is a pivotal role within a large and vibrant Faculty, providing leadership and guidance in matters of policy, strategy, change and planning. The role holder will contribute to the development of the Faculty of History, support key committees, and line manage a team professional services staff dedicated to undergraduate student administration and facilities management. The successful candidate will be educated to degree level, possess excellent organisational skills with the ability to manage and prioritise a varied workload. The ability to implement change, understand, interpret, manage and design administrative processes, together with previous experience in a senior administrative role is required. The ability to work as part of a team, providing clear leadership, plus excellent communication skills (both written and verbal) are also essential attributes for this role. Temporary cover: This post is fixed-term for 13 months or the return of the post holder, whichever is the earlier. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries about the role are welcomed and should be directed to Elizabeth Haresnape, Faculty Manager at eh273@cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact Karin Kuchta, HR Coordinator at acdhr@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference AK51396 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information AK51396 - Further Particulars Key information Department/location Academic Division Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference AK51396 Category Academic-related Date published 20 October 2026 Closing date 8 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
