    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/digital-assessment-training-and-engagement-coordinator-fixed-term-ab51490": {
      "title": "Digital Assessment Training and Engagement Coordinator (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Digital Assessment Training and Engagement Coordinator (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Digital Assessment Training and Engagement Coordinator (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Digital Assessment Training and Engagement Coordinator (Fixed Term) The Exam Operations Team sits within Student Administration in Education Services. They support the University's academic mission, providing expert operational support and advice to the University and Colleges on the delivery of examinations and reasonable adjustments for undergraduate and taught postgraduate courses. The team manages the administration of mitigating circumstances and examination allowances. About the Role The role holder will play a key role in supporting the University's transition to digital assessment and delivering a high-quality, inclusive and sustainable assessment experience.\nThe role holder will lead the engagement, training and adoption strategy for the digital assessment service, supporting the successful implementation and embedding across the Collegiate University. Working with key stakeholders, the role holder will support the rollout of the digital assessment platform Inspera within Departments and Colleges and promote effective engagement with students. \nThe postholder will work alongside the Head of Digital Launch and Programme Manager to develop and deliver training resources, communications and engagement activities that support the transition to, and ongoing operation of, digital assessment services.\nOperating across the University, the role involves collaboration with academic departments, Colleges, students, senior University committees and external partners. The role holder will provide expert advice on engagement and adoption, helping to ensure effective implementation, consistent practice and continuous service improvement. We are seeking an individual who can demonstrate: Experience of designing and delivering communications and engagement activity to support organisational change, policy implementation or institution-wide programmes involving multiple stakeholder groups. Strong knowledge of communications and stakeholder engagement, including experience of advising senior stakeholders on messaging, timing, audience engagement and reputational considerations. Experience of designing, delivering and evaluating training, workshops or learning resources for diverse audiences. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with experience of producing and quality-assuring high-impact content for varied audiences. The ability to develop practical engagement and communications strategies, establish evaluation measures, interpret audience insight and influence stakeholders through collaborative and matrix-working approaches. A degree-level qualification, or equivalent professional experience, in communications, stakeholder engagement, organisational change or a related discipline. In return we offer you: 41 days annual leave, including Bank Holidays; Access to a wide range of employee benefits, Membership of the Universities Superannuation Scheme (USS), a defined benefit pension scheme; A Personal and Professional development plan to support career growth; A hybrid work model is possible at certain times, however, the role requires some days per week in the office. During peak examination times, the role holder may need to be in the office full-time which might also include some Saturday and Bank Holiday working. Interviews will be held in person on Tuesday 23 or Wednesday 24 November 2026 in the Student Services Centre. Further information is available via the link below.\nWhen applying please upload your CV and a covering letter outlining how you meet the essential criteria set out in the Person Specification in the Further Particulars. Applications are welcome from both external and internal candidates, including internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment. Informal enquiries can be directed to jenny.green@admin.cam.ac.uk Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact SSCjobs@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference AB51490 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Student Administration Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference AB51490 Category Academic-related Date published 27 October 2026 Closing date 15 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/duty-manager-sunday-part-time-fixed-term-ve51425": {
      "title": "Duty Manager (Sunday) (Part Time, Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Duty Manager (Sunday) (Part Time, Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Duty Manager (Sunday) (Part Time, Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Duty Manager (Sunday) (Part Time, Fixed Term) Ever wanted to work in an institution that is home to one of the world's great collections of cultural treasures and research materials? Spanning thousands of years of human thought and discovery, Cambridge University Libraries and Archives house unique treasures and research materials made up of nearly ten million books, maps, manuscripts, photographs and priceless objects. The role As we expand our library availability with a new Sunday service, we are seeking a Duty Manager to oversee operations, maintain high service standards, and foster an environment where all members of our community feel supported and included. The role is available for Sundays only, for 5 hours, and is temporary until January 2028. As Duty Manager you will Provide leadership, coaching, and supervision to customer service team members during Sunday opening. Ensure the needs of Library users are consistently met or exceeded. Take a proactive, flexible approach to operational problem-solving and service quality. Monitor customer satisfaction and feed into continuous service improvement. What we are looking for Strong background in customer-focused service delivery for diverse audiences. Demonstrated experience in team leadership, coaching, or supervision. Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills. Experience within the library or information sector preferred. What we offer Generous annual leave allowance of 41 days which will be pro rata depending on days worked across the week. Exceptional parental leave (including maternity, paternity / co-parent, adoption and shared parental leave). Discounts on major retailers. Professional development opportunities such as apprenticeships and access to a variety of training courses. We particularly welcome applications from candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our department. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For informal enquiries please contact Steve Stacey, Customer Support Manager, sjs34@cam.ac.uk . Application closing date: Sunday 1 November 2026. Interview date: Tuesday 10 November 2026. For further details please refer to the Further Particulars. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 12 months in the first instance. Please quote reference VE51425 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location University Library Salary £35,608-£46,049 pro rata Reference VE51425 Category Academic-related Date published 19 October 2026 Closing date 1 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/enterprise-and-events-assistant-fixed-term-pe51325": {
      "title": "Enterprise and Events Assistant (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Enterprise and Events Assistant (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Enterprise and Events Assistant (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Enterprise and Events Assistant (Fixed Term) We are seeking an enthusiastic Enterprise and Events Assistant to support a range of commercial activities, including venue hire, project coordination, administration and stakeholder engagement. Working closely with the Assistant Director (Development and Enterprise), you will coordinate day-to-day activities, take venue hire enquiries and bookings, maintain management information and reporting, and provide administrative support across a variety of projects.  This is an excellent opportunity to develop broad experience in enterprise and commercial operations within a unique organisation. You will work with colleagues across the Garden and external stakeholders, helping to generate income and support the Garden's long-term sustainability. We are looking for someone with strong organisational and people skills, good attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities. You will be proactive, confident using your initiative, quick to learn new systems and able to keep tasks and projects moving forward. This is a new and varied role and you will need to communicate effectively with people who have different priorities and working styles. You will bring a flexible, collaborative approach and enjoy contributing to a small, supportive team. If you enjoy variety and making things happen behind the scenes, we would love to hear from you. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 3 years in the first instance, with the potential for extension subject to funding. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For any questions relating to this recruitment please contact admin@botanic.cam.ac.uk The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Botanic Garden Salary £27,319-£31,236 Reference PE51325 Category Assistant staff Date published 20 October 2026 Closing date 22 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
