    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/exams-administrator-digital-support-ab51011": {
      "title": "Exams Administrator (Digital Support)",
      "description": "Exams Administrator (Digital Support) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Exams Administrator (Digital Support) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Exams Administrator (Digital Support) The Exam Operations team are looking to recruit a conscientious team player who will contribute to our continuing success. The Team The Exam Operations team sit within the Student Administration section of Education Services, supporting the academic purposes of the University, and provides expert administrative support and advice to the University and Colleges relating to operational delivery of exams and reasonable adjustments for undergraduate and taught postgraduate courses. It also manages the administration of mitigating circumstances and allowances for undergraduate and taught postgraduate students. About the Role This role has been introduced to support with the delivery of those functions listed above with a primary focus on digital assessment and the services and support for stakeholders including students and departments. The work and activities will initially cross over between the Digital Assessment Programme (DAP) and Business as Usual (BAU). The Digital Assessment Programme is establishing a centrally supported digital examinations service for the University, enabling departments to transition appropriate handwritten, in-person summative examinations to a secure digital platform. The role will collaborate closely with colleagues across the Exam Operations team and the Digital Assessment Programme team to ensure smooth digital exam delivery. The work involved in this role will be varied and key responsibilities are included in the further particulars document. Given the role requirements, we invite applications from individuals who : are highly meticulous, accurate, and organised; are able to work under pressure and with a wide and complex workload; have good interpersonal and communication skills; have the ability to work collaboratively; are quick to adapt to change are conscientious and will contribute to the continuing success of the team; have experience of working within a digital focused role or environment In return we would offer you : generous annual leave  36 days (including Bank Holidays), a clear training plan, with supportive training being delivered by colleagues within the team; regular check in's (weekly) with your Supervisor and / or Line Manager and an annual review; a Personal and Professional development plan to encourage future growth and access to various University training courses the opportunity to network within the Student Services Centre and with Colleges, Departments and individuals across the wider University; a supportive, inclusive and engaging working environment. Interviews will be held in person on Thursday 26th November 2026 in the Student Services Centre. Further information is available via the link below. If you would like more information about the role, informal enquiries can be directed by email to jo.overhill@admin.cam.ac.uk . To apply online for this vacancy, please click on the 'Apply' button below. This will route you to the University's Web Recruitment System, where you will need to register an account (if you have not already) and log in before completing the online application form. Please quote reference AB51011 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society.\nThe University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Reference: AB51011 Closing Date: Sunday 8th November 2026 Interview Date: Thursday 26th November 2026 Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact SSCjobs@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference AB51011 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Student Administration Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference AB51011 Category Assistant staff Date published 26 October 2026 Closing date 8 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
