      "description": "Research Assistant/Associate (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant/Associate (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant/Associate (Fixed Term) Fixed-term: The post is available for 20 months in the first instance starting in January 2027, or as soon as possible thereafter, and is subject to a 6-month probationary period. Applications are invited for a Postdoctoral Research Associate position in malaria parasite biology. The position is initially funded for a 20-month term, via a BBSRC Pioneer grant held in the laboratory of Professor Catherine Merrick (Division of Microbiology and Parasitology, Department of Pathology, University of Cambridge). Pioneer grants aim to support high-risk/high-gain discovery research: this project will investigate the biology of a novel virus recently discovered in malaria parasites. It will use a range of cutting-edge techniques in molecular genetics, transcriptomics, biochemistry and cell biology in cultured Plasmodium parasites. It is hoped that the initial proof-of-concept work will lead to further grant applications, and hence to potential extension of this project. Applicants should hold (or be close to completing) a PhD in parasitology, molecular biology or biochemistry, with skills in cell culture and molecular genetics. Specific experience in any or all of the following techniques is highly desirable: Plasmodium culture and Plasmodium molecular genetics, particularly in P. knowlesi or P. falciparum; protein biochemistry; RNA-seq and transcriptomic data analysis. Relevant experience should be demonstrated by publications in peer-reviewed journals. The role requires the ability to work both independently and within a team, plus excellent communication, organizational and problem-solving skills. Other responsibilities will include developing and driving the research objectives and preparing the work for presentation, publication and follow-on funding applications. The appointee will benefit from excellent facilities, including recently-refurbished Category-3 containment laboratories, and diverse expertise at the Cambridge Pathology Department, which hosts four parasitology research groups focused on malaria and leishmania. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. Please upload your Curriculum Vitae (CV; maximum 2 pages), a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) detailing project and career development plans, and a publications list in the upload section of the online application. Please provide contact details, including email addresses, of two referees, at least one of whom should be familiar with your research in your primary research field. If you upload any additional documents not requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Appointment at the Research Associate level is dependent on the award of a PhD. Those who have submitted but not yet received their PhD will be appointed at the Research Assistant level, Grade 5 (£35,302-£36,320), which will be amended to Research Associate, Grade 7 (£38,448-£46,970) once the award of the PhD has been confirmed. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to: Prof Merrick at cjm48@cam.ac.uk . Queries regarding the application process, should be directed to HR: hr@path.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference PK51454 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Pathology Salary £34,610-£35,608 £37,694-£46,049 Reference PK51454 Category Research Date published 20 October 2026 Closing date 15 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-assistantassociate-in-carbon-assessment-and-efficiency-improvement-fixed-term-nm51509": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Associate in Carbon Assessment and Efficiency Improvement (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Assistant/Associate in Carbon Assessment and Efficiency Improvement (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant/Associate in Carbon Assessment and Efficiency Improvement (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant/Associate in Carbon Assessment and Efficiency Improvement (Fixed Term) A position exists for a Research Assistant/Associate in the Department of Engineering to work on the REWIRE Project. The post holder will be located at the Institute for Manufacturing in West Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, UK. The role holder will interact directly with research collaborators including Neutreeno and six UK SMEs in the electronics industry, lead the required tasks in Work Package 1b, and undertake assigned tasks in Work Packages 2, 3 and 4. Key responsibilities include coordinating the REWIRE Project with Neutreeno, the SME collaborators and colleagues within CUED; reviewing carbon assessment methodologies and systems; understanding SME issues and requirements for CO2 emission assessment and efficiency improvement; co-developing an effective system for SMEs with Neutreeno; organising workshops; engaging wider SME communities to disseminate the system and associated best practices; and planning and controlling the project from the University of Cambridge side. The role holder will also collaborate with IfM scholars and students to develop an education case for ISMM/MET, academic papers on CO2 emission assessment and efficiency improvement, and research grant proposals for EPSRC and/or other research councils. Applicants must have, or be close to obtaining, a PhD in a relevant discipline, or equivalent experience. Applicants should demonstrate knowledge of carbon assessment methodologies and systems, the ability to understand the requirements of SMEs in the electronics industry, experience of collaborative research and project coordination, and excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Appointment at Research Associate level is dependent on having a PhD, or equivalent experience. Those who have submitted but not yet received their PhD will be appointed at Research Assistant level, which will be amended to Research Associate once the PhD has been awarded. Salary ranges: Research Assistant: £33,662 - £36,320\nResearch Associate: £38,448 - £46,970 Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available until 31 March 2027 in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload your Curriculum Vitae (CV) and a covering letter in the Upload section of the online application. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please submit your application by midnight on the closing date. If you have any questions about this vacancy, please contact Professor Yongjiang Shi. For questions about the application process, please contact the Process Administrator, Rebecca Evans ( rhf31@cam.ac.uk ). Please quote reference NM51509 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information HR7 Research Assistant/Associate in Carbon Assessment and Efficiency Improvement Key information Department/location Department of Engineering Salary £33,662-£36,320 £38,448-£46,049 Reference NM51509 Category Research Date published 26 October 2026 Closing date 9 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
