    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/senior-accounts-clerk-rr51479": {
      "title": "Senior Accounts Clerk",
      "description": "Senior Accounts Clerk | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Senior Accounts Clerk Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Senior Accounts Clerk Positioned at the Cambridge Biomedical Campus, the Department of Clinical Neurosciences is leading medical discovery into neurosciences. Our mission is both profound and urgent: to improve the lives of people with neurological illness and injury through discovery, innovative treatments and training of the next generation. We are seeking a Senior Accounts Clerk to join our professional services finance team at an exciting time as we move towards a new finance system. This is a varied and important role supporting the day-to-day financial administration of a large, research-active department, including purchasing, accounts payable and receivable, research grants, general ledger activity, financial record keeping and support for finance system users. Working closely with the Finance Manager, Finance Coordinator and Grants Coordinator, you will help ensure that finance processes are accurate, timely and compliant with University procedures. The role will involve liaising with colleagues across the Department, the School and central University teams, as well as supporting activity connected with the Wolfson Brain Imaging Centre (WBIC), a major research facility. This is an excellent opportunity for someone with experience in a busy accounts environment who enjoys working with detail, solving practical problems and providing helpful, responsive support to others. You will contribute to clear and compliant financial administration across a complex portfolio of activity, including research funding, core budgets, donations, and operational accounts. We are looking for a well-organised and proactive individual with strong communication skills, good attention to detail and confidence using Microsoft Office, particularly Excel and SharePoint. You will be comfortable managing competing deadlines, working as part of a supportive team and building positive working relationships with academic, research and professional services colleagues. Experience of University finance systems, iProcurement or Oracle Fusion would be helpful, but a flexible approach and willingness to learn are equally important. Informal enquiries about the position can be submitted by email to Hanli Schmidt, Finance Coordinator, hv268@cam.ac.uk We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time (minimum 0.6 FTE) working or other flexible working arrangements. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role on the online application form. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Closing Date: 15th November 2026 Interviews will likely take place 2-3 weeks after the advert has closed Please quote reference RR51479 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Clinical Neurosciences Salary £27,319-£31,236 Reference RR51479 Category Assistant staff Date published 22 October 2026 Closing date 15 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
