      "title": "Senior Change and Engagement Manager",
      "description": "Senior Change and Engagement Manager | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Senior Change and Engagement Manager Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Senior Change and Engagement Manager The Role This is an opportunity to play a leading role in a significant transformation programme at the University of Cambridge. The Finance Transformation Programme (FTP) is seeking a Senior Change Manager to join its Change and Engagement Team, helping to shape how colleagues across the University experience and adopt change. Your Skills In this fixed-term role, with line management responsibilities, you will lead the Change and Engagement Team in preparing finance and non-finance colleagues for the transition to new systems, processes and ways of working. Your focus will be on ensuring colleagues feel informed, supported and confident throughout the transformation journey. Working across a complex and diverse organisation, you will guide change readiness activities, engage with stakeholders at all levels, and help validate the impacts and benefits of the transformation with end users. You will support the successful introduction of Oracle Fusion and new financial ways of working, ensuring that the needs and perspectives of colleagues are reflected throughout delivery. The role offers significant opportunities to collaborate with programme leaders, operational teams, and specialist Training and Communications colleagues. It is ideally suited to a change professional who enjoys building relationships, leading teams, and helping organisations navigate large-scale transformation with confidence and clarity. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available until 31 December 2027 in the first instance. The post is offered to internal candidates only on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. Benefits The University offers an excellent benefit package including: 41 days annual leave, inclusive of Bank Holidays Defined benefits pension schemes Flexible working options Family-friendly initiatives Career development opportunities Support for health & mental wellbeing Discounts on shopping Rental deposit scheme Public transport season ticket loans Tax-efficient bicycle and charity-giving schemes Location The University is supportive of hybrid working, where some work is undertaken on University premises and some in a remote working environment. The aim of our approach is to enable as many staff as possible to work in a hybrid way if they wish and where their role allows. This arrangement is subject to change and will not form a part of the contractual terms of the role. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you would like more information about this role, informal enquiries can be directed by email to Alistair Catterall, FTP Change Lead via email at Alistair.Catterall@admin.cam.ac.uk If you have any questions the application process, please contact a Recruitment Administrator at Finhr_recruitment@admin.cam.ac.uk . The closing date for applications is 06 November 2026. The interviews date for the role are planned 18 November 2026. Please quote reference AG51438 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Senior Change and E Key information Department/location Finance Division Salary £47,389-£59,966 Reference AG51438 Category Academic-related Date published 20 October 2026 Closing date 6 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/senior-collections-assistant-centre-for-material-culture-part-time-fixed-term-internal-application-ju51465": {
      "title": "Senior Collections Assistant (Centre for Material Culture) Part Time, Fixed Term",
      "description": "Senior Collections Assistant (Centre for Material Culture) Part Time, Fixed Term - (Internal application only) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Senior Collections Assistant (Centre for Material Culture) Part Time, Fixed Term - (Internal application only) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Senior Collections Assistant (Centre for Material Culture) Part Time, Fixed Term - (Internal application only) Internal application only The Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology is seeking to appoint a Senior Collections Assistant (Centre for Material Culture). The role holder will promote and support Higher Education collections-based teaching at the MAA's Centre for Material Culture (CMC). From 2025 this facility provides an opportunity to enable collections access for a wide range of University courses. With the guidance of the Director and Curators, the role holder will establish and maintain connections with a range of academic departments. They will liaise with departmental staff to identify opportunities for teaching, support student access and assist with programming sessions. The role holder will work effectively with the wider MAA collections team as well as support MAA learning staff, including the Senior Education and Outreach Assistant (Centre for Material Culture), and others who work from this site. The Museum is the second largest of the University of Cambridge's eight museums and is both a museum open to the general public and a research and teaching facility of the University. The Museum is open to the public Tuesdays to Sundays and welcomes over 100,000 visitors a year. Please see the further particulars document for full information on the role responsibilities and person specification. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available until 30 June 2027 in the first instance. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. MAA and the University of Cambridge Museums are committed to inclusion and diversity within our institutions and across the sector, and we particularly welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic candidates as they are under-represented within the Museum and the University. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries about this vacancy may be addressed Imogen Gunn, Collections Manager (Archaeology) ilg22@cam.ac.uk and Rachel Hand, Collections Manager (Anthropology) rh259@cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact Faculty HR at hr@hsps.cam.ac.uk The closing date for applications is Wednesday 04 November 2026 with in-person interviews on Tuesday 10 November 2026. Please quote reference JU51465 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology Salary £31,236-£35,608 pro rata Reference JU51465 Category Assistant staff Date published 21 October 2026 Closing date 4 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/senior-lead-strategic-change-yv51401": {
      "title": "Senior Lead: Strategic Change",
      "description": "Senior Lead: Strategic Change | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Senior Lead: Strategic Change Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Senior Lead: Strategic Change Limited funding: The funds for this post are available for 3 years in the first instance. University of Cambridge The University of Cambridge is one of the world's leading universities, renowned for excellence in research, teaching and innovation. As the University continues to invest in major transformation programmes that will shape its future operating model, we are seeking an exceptional strategic change leader to join the newly established University Change Support Office (UCSO). The UCSO has been created to provide critical expertise in change management, engagement, communications, benefits realisation, portfolio planning and programme governance across the University's portfolio of major change initiatives. The Role This is a high-profile leadership role responsible for defining and embedding the University's approach to change management, ensuring that major initiatives are aligned through a coherent strategy, consistent standards and effective governance arrangements. You will work closely with senior leaders, programme sponsors, Schools, Institutions and professional service teams to build organisational capability, strengthen change sponsorship and support the successful delivery of transformational outcomes. Key responsibilities include: Leading the development, implementation and ongoing evolution of the University's Change Strategy Establishing standards, governance frameworks and measures for major change activity across the institution Acting as the University's senior adviser on strategic change, organisational readiness and stakeholder engagement Building strong relationships with senior leaders, programme sponsors and governance bodies to influence successful change outcomes Leading the development of long-term change capability across the University, including training, development and career pathways Creating and sustaining strategic change networks that support collaboration, knowledge sharing and best practice Overseeing the evaluation of change impact, stakeholder sentiment and benefits realisation Supporting the design and implementation of new operating models and organisational change initiatives Developing business cases and strategic plans for the future evolution of change management across the University About You You will be an accomplished strategic change professional with extensive experience leading large-scale organisational transformation within a complex environment. You will combine deep expertise in change management with strong leadership capability, political awareness and exceptional stakeholder engagement skills. Comfortable operating at executive level, you will have a proven ability to influence senior stakeholders and build consensus across diverse groups. You will be highly collaborative, able to navigate complexity and committed to delivering sustainable organisational change. We are particularly interested in candidates who can demonstrate: Significant experience leading major organisational change and transformation programmes Experience influencing senior stakeholders and operating effectively within complex, devolved organisations A strong track record of shaping and delivering organisation-wide strategy, policy and practice Proven leadership and people management experience Expertise in change management, engagement and communications Excellent relationship-building, influencing and stakeholder management skills The ability to build organisational capability and foster long-term cultural change Why Join the University Change Support Office? You will play a leading role in delivering transformational change across the University, working with senior leaders to drive sustainable improvements and shape the institution's future success. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Applications must include a CV and a covering letter. The closing date for applications is midnight on Friday 13 November 2026. Interviews are expected to take place on Thursday 10 December 2026. We reserve the right to close this vacancy early if we receive sufficient applications for the role. Therefore, if you are interested, please submit your application as early as possible. Informal enquiries regarding this position can be made to: John Dennis, Director of Transformation Programmes ( jsd3@cam.ac.uk ) If you have any queries about the recruitment process, please contact Caitlin Misso, Recruitment Coordinator, Senior Professional Appointments ( Caitlin.Misso@admin.cam.ac.uk ) Please quote reference YV51401 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Document Key information Department/location University Change Support Office Salary £82,932-£105,009 Reference YV51401 Category Academic-related Date published 21 October 2026 Closing date 13 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/senior-programme-manager-ag51463": {
      "title": "Senior Programme Manager",
      "description": "Senior Programme Manager | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Senior Programme Manager Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Senior Programme Manager We reserve the right to close this vacancy early if we receive sufficient applications for the role. Therefore, if you are interested, please submit your application as early as possible. The implementation of the new finance system is a once in a lifetime opportunity to make a difference to the way in which University departments process and manage their financial transactions. We are looking for an experienced Senior Programme Manager to play a pivotal leadership role in delivering this transformation. You will provide strategic oversight and end-to-end delivery leadership across major, complex and interdependent areas of the programme, ensuring that plans are achievable, risks and dependencies are actively managed, and delivery remains aligned with the University's strategic objectives. The Role Working closely with Executive Sponsors, senior University leaders, business teams, technical specialists and external delivery partners, you will lead the planning and delivery of key programme initiatives, bringing together business, technology and change activities to achieve successful outcomes. You will operate across a complex stakeholder environment, providing the leadership, structure and governance needed to maintain momentum, resolve challenges and manage competing priorities. This will include overseeing programme plans, resources, budgets, risks, issues and dependencies, ensuring that progress is clearly understood and that decisions are taken at the right level and at the right time. Through strong leadership and governance, the role will help ensure the successful realisation of programme objectives and the delivery of sustainable transformational change. Your Skills You will be an experienced programme or senior project management professional with a strong track record of delivering complex, large-scale transformation initiatives in a challenging stakeholder environment. You will combine strategic thinking with a pragmatic, delivery-focused approach, knowing how to translate ambitious objectives into realistic plans and tangible results. You will hold a professional qualification alongside a project management qualification and have excellent inter-personal, analytical and communication skills. Alongside these you will possess: Excellent planning for short, medium and long term using MS Projects A good understanding of enterprise systems and business transformation, ideally with experience of Oracle Financials or Oracle Fusion implementations. Identify and pro-actively manage important risks, issues and problems effectively. Experience of working within a large, complex organisation, particularly in higher education or a similarly diverse institutional environment, would be advantageous. Benefits The University offers an excellent benefit package including: 41 days annual leave, inclusive of Bank Holidays Defined benefits pension schemes Flexible working options Career development opportunities Support for health and mental wellbeing Discounts on shopping Location The University is supportive of hybrid working, where some work is undertaken on University premises and some in a remote working environment. The aim of our approach is to enable as many staff as possible to work in a hybrid way if they wish and where their role allows. This arrangement is subject to change and will not form a part of the contractual terms of the role. Funding for this post is available for 12 months. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check, a health assessment and a security check. If you would like more information about this role, informal enquiries can be directed by email to Michelle Bond on Michelle.Bond@admin.cam.ac.uk . If you have any questions the application process, please contact a Recruitment Administrator at Finhr_recruitment@admin.cam.ac.uk . The closing date for applications is 5 November 2026. The interview date for the role is 17 November 2026. Please quote reference AG51463 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Senior Programme Manager Key information Department/location Finance Division Salary £69,488 Reference AG51463 Category Academic-related Date published 21 October 2026 Closing date 5 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/strategic-operations-lead-this-institute-fixed-term-rh51520": {
      "title": "Strategic Operations Lead THIS Institute (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Strategic Operations Lead THIS Institute (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Strategic Operations Lead THIS Institute (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Strategic Operations Lead THIS Institute (Fixed Term) The Strategic Operations Lead at THIS Institute is a senior leadership role central to the Institute's mission to build a strong evidence base for improving and innovating in healthcare. As a key member of the Institute's executive team, the post-holder will provide strategic and operational leadership across business planning, finance, governance, risk, human resources, contracting, funding applications, research programme management, impact and continuous improvement. They will lead a multi-skilled team and work with stakeholders across the NHS, academia, charities, professional bodies and the wider University. The role requires the ability to interpret complex organisational objectives and translate them into effective plans, systems and processes while working within University of Cambridge requirements. This will include managing complex budgets of approximately £3-4 million per year, producing accurate forecasts and management information, maintaining effective financial controls and compliance, and presenting clear analysis and recommendations to senior leaders and governance committees. The role will also require oversight of governance, risk management, business planning and reporting. The post-holder will be a credible and collaborative senior leader with excellent judgement and strong analytical, facilitation and negotiation skills. They will be highly organised, proactive and self-directed, able to plan for the long term, prioritise competing demands and remain composed in a fast-paced environment. They will have significant experience of leading people and teams, promoting an inclusive and positive working culture, and ensuring high standards of human resource management. Educated to honours degree level, and ideally holding a relevant postgraduate qualification, the successful candidate will have extensive experience of operations and business leadership, including the delivery of complex, multi-stakeholder programmes. Funding for this post is available until 31 July 2030 in the first instance. This is a full-time position. Location: Department of Public Health and Primary Care, Strangeways Research Laboratory, Worts Causeway, Cambridge CB1 8RN (approximately two miles south of the city centre). Informal enquiries may be directed to Rachael Comeau at phpc.hr@medschl.cam.ac.uk Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter and CV in the Upload section of the online application. The covering letter should outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Closing Date: 10th November 2026 Interview Date: 18th November 2026 Please quote reference RH51520 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Department of Public Health and Primary Care, THIS Institute Salary £48,337 - £61,165 Reference RH51520 Category Academic-related Date published 27 October 2026 Closing date 10 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/teaching-associate-in-philosophy-temporary-cover-gv51456": {
      "title": "Teaching Associate in Philosophy [Temporary Cover]",
      "description": "Teaching Associate in Philosophy [Temporary Cover] | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Teaching Associate in Philosophy [Temporary Cover] Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Teaching Associate in Philosophy [Temporary Cover] The Faculty of Philosophy is seeking to appoint a Teaching Associate in Philosophy to provide temporary cover for a period of 20 months from 4 January 2027, or as soon as possible thereafter. The role holder will be based in the Faculty of Philosophy in Cambridge. The successful candidate will hold a philosophy PhD or be awarded their PhD by the beginning of the appointment. We expect the successful applicant to be actively pursuing research in Philosophy. This post requires teaching expertise that is at the forefront of academic practice. Ability to teach central topics, including Frege at 2nd-year level, and 1st and 2nd order logic at 3rd-year level, as well as other courses in logic or related areas to be agreed at undergraduate and master's level is essential. The ability to teach in other areas would be an advantage. The person appointed will be required to give up to 40 lectures during the academic year (24 lectures during the first, partial academic year of the appointment), to supervise MPhil students, to examine at both undergraduate and MPhil level, and to contribute to the administrative functions of the faculty. The successful applicant will also have the opportunity to participate in College teaching for additional remuneration. The undergraduate syllabus (Guide to Courses) can be found on the Faculty's website.\nIn order for your application to be considered, please upload the following: Covering letter outlining your suitability for the role Curriculum Vitae (CV) The names and contact details to two referees who are familiar with your work If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Informal enquiries about the role are welcomed and should be directed to Professor Michael Potter on mdp10@cam.ac.uk . For questions on the application process, please contact the School's HR Team on sahhr@admin.cam.ac.uk . The closing date for applications is midnight (GMT) on Monday, 16 November 2026.  Interviews are planned for Monday, 30 November 2026, subject to change. References for shortlisted candidates will be sought in the week commencing Monday, 23 November 2026; candidates are asked to inform their referees accordingly. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please quote reference GV51456 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Faculty of Philosophy Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference GV51456 Category Academic Date published 27 October 2026 Closing date 16 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/technical-specialist-instrumentation-and-electronics-nm50635": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist (Instrumentation and Electronics)",
      "description": "Technical Specialist (Instrumentation and Electronics) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Technical Specialist (Instrumentation and Electronics) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Technical Specialist (Instrumentation and Electronics) This role is based in the Department's Civil Engineering Building in West Cambridge and will provide technical support across the Division for the Civil Engineering disciplines it supports in Structures, Geotechnics and Construction. As the Technical Specialist, you will be the key technical resource for electronic and instrumentation elements of projects and will provide technical guidance to other laboratory technicians as well as provide oversight of technical projects as assigned by the Divisional Laboratory Manager. You will be a technical focal point for the Division's Technician support and will ensure that current and future research and teaching activities/needs are met to the highest standards, which includes supporting the smooth and safe running of the facility. You will report to the Divisional Laboratory Manager and work in conjunction with the Departmental Head of Design and Technical Services to provide the required highly specialised technical support service to research and/or teaching staff.  You will also provide cover for the Laboratory Manager during periods of absence as well as support the training of apprentices. The successful applicant will hold a degree in a relevant research area/ Level 6 vocational qualifications or possess an equivalent level of practical experience and be able to demonstrate a high degree of competency in the use of instrumentation and electronic equipment in a research environment. You will have specialist knowledge and skills in electronics and instrumentation as well as a good knowledge of analysis techniques. You will have strong written and verbal communication skills with proven experience of dealing with a variety of research projects and communicating research results to a wide variety of audiences as well as experience of implementing health and safety requirements within a research environment.  Previous experience of providing training to groups and individuals is also a requirement for this role. If you think you are the right candidate for the role, we would love to hear from you. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. The closing date for applications is Monday 2 November 2026. Informal enquiries are welcomed and if you have any queries regarding either the vacancy or the application process, please contact the HR Office in the first instance on hr-office@eng.cam.ac.uk or 01223 332615 Please quote reference NM50635 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Engineering Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference NM50635 Category Academic-related Date published 19 October 2026 Closing date 2 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/university-assistantassociate-professor-in-artificial-intelligence-and-machine-learning-nr49860": {
      "title": "University Assistant/Associate Professor in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning",
      "description": "University Assistant/Associate Professor in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs University Assistant/Associate Professor in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs University Assistant/Associate Professor in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning The Department of Computer Science and Technology is seeking to recruit a new faculty member at the Assistant Professor/Associate Professor level who will contribute to research and teaching in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning. We are looking for a candidate with outstanding research credentials in fundamental machine learning, who is actively questioning and rethinking the current status-quo in AI and who will make significant contributions to the next generation of novel models, abstractions and architectures.  Example specialist areas may include, but are not limited to, post-transformer architectures, continuous learning models, probabilistic machine learning and uncertainty quantification, causal machine learning, learning theory, methods bridging statistical learning and symbolic reasoning, probabilistic numerics, robust and certifiable machine learning, and foundational ML methods for scientific discovery. Candidates will have evidence of an independent research agenda, a strong publication record, international visibility, documented evidence of community service and evidence of impact commensurate with career stage and able to supervise research at both Masters and PhD level.  Teaching experience is essential and the appointee will be expected to develop innovative graduate content within the MPhil in Advanced Computer Science, and advance the curriculum and contribute to undergraduate teaching in machine learning and mathematics. The ability to secure research funding to support their vision and build a world-class team is essential. We welcome applications from researchers with interdisciplinary interests who will collaborate across different subdisciplines in Computer Science and with other academic fields (e.g., mathematics, engineering, physics, chemistry, etc.). The Department is strongly research-oriented and has long-standing strengths across a range of topics in computer science. In recent years the department has focused on building a strong presence within machine learning. The Department benefits from the machine learning ecosystem across Cambridge with strong collaborations with especially Engineering, Mathematics and Physics. All members of the Department are supported in developing their research leadership. We provide administrative support across research management, funding, communications, finance, and recruitment, and benefit from strong university-wide initiatives in commercialization, collaboration, ethics, and interdisciplinary centres. Please ensure that you upload the application documentation in PDF format as follows: Curriculum vitae, including a complete list of publications. Research statement. Please provide one or two examples of research work that you feel best represent you as a researcher and your contributions to the field. These may be publications or other research outputs. You may upload a pdf of the work, or simply include references at the end of your research statement. Teaching statement. Cover letter. Please see the Further Particulars document for details of expectations of research, teaching, and other aspects of the role. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Interviews will take place in Cambridge on 3rd and 4th March 2027. The successful candidate will join the Department on 1st September 2027, or as soon as possible thereafter. Interested applicants are encouraged to make informal enquiries about the post to Professor Robert Mullins at aiml-enquiries@cst.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference NR49860 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information University Assistant/Associate Professor in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Key information Department/location Department of Computer Science and Technology Salary £48,337 - £61,165 £64,878 - £68,817 Reference NR49860 Category Academic Date published 20 October 2026 Closing date 15 December 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/urological-malignancies-administration-assistant-part-time-fixed-term-re51492": {
      "title": "Urological Malignancies Administration Assistant (Part Time, Fixed Term)",
