    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-support-assistant-nihr-bioresource-for-translational-research-rw51545": {
      "title": "Research Support Assistant, NIHR BioResource for Translational Research",
      "description": "Research Support Assistant, NIHR BioResource for Translational Research | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Support Assistant, NIHR BioResource for Translational Research Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Support Assistant, NIHR BioResource for Translational Research Do you have great IT and organisational skills?  Interested in a role which is contributing to changing lives for the better? Looking for your next challenge? We are recruiting a Research Support Assistant who has excellent planning, organisational and attention to detail skills.  You will need to be highly competent in word processing, excel and able to learn bespoke databases for data entry and data integrity checking to succeed in this role. About NIHR BioResource: Our mission is to facilitate human health research and its transformation into medical practice. NIHR BioResource is a unique and powerful resource for studying disease mechanisms and for investigating the links between genes, the environment, health and disease, enabling scientific discoveries as well as facilitating translational medicine for the benefit of patients. Further details on the NIHR BioResource, including some of our COVID-19 research studies, can be found on our website https://bioresource.nihr.ac.uk . About the job: The Research Support Assistant supports the NIHR BioResource Clinical Team with the day-to-day running of the Clinical Research Unit under the supervision of the Research Delivery Manager in order to ensure that the unit is fully operational, up-to-date and meets all requirements of a CUH clinical area. The team (Research Nurses) provides clinical support to the NIHR BioResource in the recruitment and recall of volunteers. The role holder provides administrative and organisational support to the Clinical Team in order to ensure successful volunteer recruitment and recall for a variety of research projects. This role is key to the preparation of research appointments, including the paperwork required, as well as taking responsibility for welcoming volunteers to the unit; all of which will influence the volunteer's research experience. About you: Ideally you will have: Education to A Level standard with GCSE Mathematics and English or have equivalent qualifications or equivalent experience Excellent interpersonal skills to be able to greet volunteers and answer questions from research volunteers via phone call and email as required Experience in document control and of inputting data accurately What we offer: The University offers a wide range of benefits including flexible working, family friendly policies, an attractive pension scheme (employer's contribution is 12.6%). and 36 days' annual holiday (inclusive of public holidays). We encourage career development by providing extensive training & development opportunities. This appointment is part-time, 25 hours per week, Monday to Friday. Work ¿ life balance is important, and we are open to discussion on flexible working. The post is available on a fixed-term basis until 31 March 2028 in the first instance. NIHR BioResource is funded by the National Institute for Health & Care Research (NIHR) on a 4-year funding cycle. Our offices are on the Cambridge Biomedical Campus CB2 0QQ (approximately 2 miles south of the city centre). See the Further Information link below for full details and Person Specification. This appointment requires a Research Passport application. We encourage informal queries about the job or the application process - please contact Katie Mills, Research Delivery Manager, Katie.Mills@bioresource.nihr.ac.uk . Limited funding: The funds for this post are available until 31 March 2028 in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role on the online application form. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference RW51545 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars (RW51545) Key information Department/location Department of Haematology, NIHR BioResource Research Group Salary £27,865-£31,861 pro rata Reference RW51545 Category Assistant staff Date published 29 October 2026 Closing date 19 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/senior-hr-business-partner-department-of-engineering-internal-applicants-only-ah51529": {
      "title": "Senior HR Business Partner (Department of Engineering) Internal Applicants Only",
      "description": "Senior HR Business Partner (Department of Engineering) Internal Applicants Only | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Senior HR Business Partner (Department of Engineering) Internal Applicants Only Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Senior HR Business Partner (Department of Engineering) Internal Applicants Only Are you an accomplished HR professional with a proven track record in people management, driving high-performing teams, and delivering innovative, high-quality HR services? The Department of Engineering, at the University of Cambridge, is seeking a strategic and dynamic Senior HR Business Partner (SHRBP) to join our dedicated HR team. About the Role Reporting to the Lead HR Business Partner for the School of Technology, this important role is fully embedded within the Department of Engineering and leads a team of 14 dedicated HR professionals delivering a range of HR functions including business partnering, case management, resourcing and HR administration services. The Department of Engineering is the largest within the University of Cambridge (approximately 800 staff) and operates across a diverse range of Academic and Professional Services divisions. As SHRBP, you will play a pivotal role in shaping and delivering the people plans for the Department. Leading the development and implementation of the Department's HR plan, you will ensure alignment with the Department's academic vision, the School of Technology's priorities, and the University's People Strategy. Providing both strategic and operational leadership, you will oversee the delivery of high-quality HR business partnering, resourcing and HR administration services. You will lead and develop a dedicated team of 14 HR professionals, fostering a culture of excellence, collaboration and continuous improvement. Working closely with senior academic and professional services leaders, you will develop workforce and people plans that support the Department's evolving priorities and long-term success. As a member of the Department's Senior Leadership Team, you will work collaboratively with colleagues across the HR Division, including the University's central HR Business Partnering Team. You will represent the Department's interests in the development of University-wide HR policies and people initiatives, ensuring departmental perspectives and operational requirements help shape institutional approaches. The role has responsibility for leading key people initiatives in the Department of Engineering across areas including workforce planning, recruitment, equality, diversity and inclusion, pay and reward, and organisational development. You will champion innovative, evidence-based HR solutions that enable the Department to achieve its strategic objectives, while building strong and trusted relationships with stakeholders across the Department and University. What You'll Bring We are looking for an HR professional with: Strong management and leadership skills, with experience of operating in a complex matrix organisation Well-developed communication, influencing, coaching and negotiation skills The ability to develop and deliver HR plans and workforce planning Strong influencing skills Substantial experience in managing complex employee relations matters and strategic organisational change management Be part of a team making a real impact in one of the world's leading academic and research institutions. The department offers a welcoming and inclusive environment, and the opportunity to work alongside supportive and collaborative colleagues. For more information about the department, please visit: https://www.eng.cam.ac.uk/ Benefits of working at the University include: 41 days' annual leave (inclusive of bank holidays and University closure days) Generous defined benefit pension scheme Enhanced family leave and pay policies Hybrid and flexible working arrangements Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Closing date for applications: Midnight, Wednesday 11 November 2026 Interviews for the role will be held: 17 November 2026 Please quote reference AH51529 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Human Resources Division Salary £48,337-£61,165 Reference AH51529 Category Academic-related Date published 29 October 2026 Closing date 11 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/senior-research-associate-solid-state-nmr-fixed-term-ma51550": {
      "title": "Senior Research Associate: Solid-state NMR (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Senior Research Associate: Solid-state NMR (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Senior Research Associate: Solid-state NMR  (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Senior Research Associate: Solid-state NMR  (Fixed Term) Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 22 months in the first instance. Applications are invited for a senior post-doctoral research associate to join the group of Prof. Alexander Forse at the Department of Chemistry at the University of Cambridge. Essential requirement: candidates must have (or be about to obtain) a PhD in solid-state NMR spectroscopy, and at least 3 years post-doc experience (or equivalent in industry) in NMR spectroscopy. Please detail in your cover letter how you experience matches the responsibilities of this role: leading/managing the NMR facility in the Forse Group independently developing new magnetic resonance approaches to study materials for climate change mitigation leading on student training and development in magnetic resonance, and co-supervising PhD students supporting research proposal development This project is part of an ERC starting grant (funded by UKRI) which seeks to understand and improve supercapacitor devices for energy storage, with a focus on using solid-state NMR techniques to gain structural insights. Research more generally in the Forse group centers around the development of new materials for climate change mitigation. The successful applicant will benefit from access to 400 and 600 MHz NMR spectrometers (Bruker), potentiostats for electrochemistry measurements, gas sorption instruments, and diffraction resources, as required for this project. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload your Curriculum Vitae (CV), a covering letter and publications list in the upload section of the online application. If you upload any additional documents that have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. For informal enquiries, please contact Professor A Forse - acf50@cam.ac.uk Please quote reference MA51550 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The School of Physical Sciences holds an Athena Swan Silver Award which recognises and supports progress in gender equality. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further information Key information Department/location Yusuf Hamied Department of Chemistry Salary £43,099-£57,666 Reference MA51550 Category Research Date published 29 October 2026 Closing date 12 November 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
