      "title": "University Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University Assistant Professor | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs University Assistant Professor Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs University Assistant Professor The Institute of Criminology at the University of Cambridge is one of the oldest Institutes of Criminology in Europe, it is also among the strongest criminology departments globally with respect to the scope and impact of its research, the quality of its academic support infrastructure, and the talent of its students. Due to increasing student numbers, we seek to appoint two Assistant Professors, who will be joining a thriving and diverse community that is dedicated to excellence in research and teaching. We are seeking applicants who can demonstrate the capacity to conduct innovative research of international stature and contribute to teaching in the following areas: Interventions and Evaluations (broadly defined), or Crime and Criminal Justice Policy (also broadly defined). Details on the specific experience required for each can be found in the attached further particulars document. We are particularly interested in applicants who can demonstrate the ability to develop and apply innovative theoretical perspectives and methodological approaches. We are not committed to any particular methodological perspective for either post, and welcome high-quality research drawing on quantitative, qualitative, experimental, comparative, computational, ethnographic, digital, mixed methodologies, and other approaches appropriate to the research topic. You will join us with a PhD or an equivalent postgraduate qualification in criminology or a cognate discipline (e.g. psychology, psychiatry, sociology, anthropology, political science, economics, law, philosophy, and related social and behavioural sciences). You will have an established or developing bibliography of research publications and demonstrate the vision, leadership and enthusiasm to develop and secure funding for a research programme of international stature in your field. As Assistant Professor, you will contribute to our vibrant and diverse teaching programmes including the development, management and delivery of graduate and undergraduate courses, supervision, and examinations. At a later stage, you will be expected to contribute to the administration of the Institute. Applicants should submit: a) A CV b) Cover letter with: An indication whether you wish to be considered for the 'Interventions and Evaluations' or the 'Crime and Criminal Justice Policy' position, detailing your expertise in the chosen specialism. We also encourage applications from candidates with expertise across both domains, who should feel free to apply either for the position that better fits them, or for both positions. A statement covering your current and future aspirations for research and teaching, identifying, where possible, how these fit within the current research profile of the Institute (max 1000 words). A brief summary of up to three outputs you consider the most significant (max 300 words per output). A list of publications. Contact details of three referees. Appointments will be made at Assistant Professor level with a probationary period of five years. If successful at probation, the title becomes Associate Professor, with appointment to the retiring age thereafter subject to satisfactory progress. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries can be directed to Professor Leo Zaibert ( director@crim.cam.ac.uk ). Interviews are planned for Spring 2026 (dates tbc) Please quote reference JL51517 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information UTO Scheme Further Particulars Key information Department/location Institute of Criminology Salary £48,337-£61,165 Reference JL51517 Category Academic Date published 29 October 2026 Closing date 3 January 2027 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    }
  },
